  {"id":30,"x":260,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Wild Rose Thicket","descriptions":["Pale pink roses blossom against thorny green leaves, growing in profusion in the dense thicket.  The trail twists and turns, following the hoofprints of countless generations of deer.  An intense fragrance perfumes the air, but all the roses in the world can't conceal the sickly-sweet stench of rotting meat that underlies it."],"exits":[{"to":28,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":31,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":31,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":31,"x":280,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Wild Rose Thicket","descriptions":["Pale pink roses blossom against thorny green leaves, growing in profusion in the dense thicket.  The trail twists and turns, following the hoofprints of countless generations of deer.  An intense fragrance perfumes the air, but all the roses in the world can't conceal the sickly-sweet stench of rotting meat that underlies it."],"exits":[{"to":30,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":32,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":30,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":32,"x":300,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Wild Rose Thicket","descriptions":["Pale pink roses blossom against thorny green leaves, growing in profusion in the dense thicket.  The trail twists and turns, following the hoofprints of countless generations of deer.  An intense fragrance perfumes the air, but all the roses in the world can't conceal the sickly-sweet stench of rotting meat that underlies it."],"exits":[{"to":31,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":33,"x":180,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Outside a Ruined Village","descriptions":["Briar roses grow in profusion around the palisade walls of a small village.  Sweetly scented as they are, nothing can mask the stench of rotting meat that emanates from the charnel heap of dead and decaying carcasses piled outside the gate.  Scraps of flesh cling to the gnawed bones of deer, wild boar and an unfortunate Human or two."],"exits":[{"to":29,"exit":"go","move":"go rose thicket"},{"to":59,"exit":"go","move":"go village gate"}]},
  {"id":34,"x":260,"y":230,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Wild Rose Thicket","descriptions":["Pale pink roses blossom against thorny green leaves, growing in profusion in the dense thicket.  The trail twists and turns, following the hoofprints of countless generations of deer.  An intense fragrance perfumes the air, but all the roses in the world can't conceal the sickly-sweet stench of rotting meat that underlies it."],"exits":[{"to":35,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":27,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":36,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":35,"x":300,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Wild Rose Thicket","descriptions":["Pale pink roses blossom against thorny green leaves, growing in profusion in the dense thicket.  The trail twists and turns, following the hoofprints of countless generations of deer.  An intense fragrance perfumes the air, but all the roses in the world can't conceal the sickly-sweet stench of rotting meat that underlies it."],"exits":[{"to":34,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":36,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":43,"exit":"go","move":"go gap"}]},
  {"id":36,"x":260,"y":190,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Wild Rose Thicket","descriptions":["Pale pink roses blossom against thorny green leaves, growing in profusion in the dense thicket.  The trail twists and turns, following the hoofprints of countless generations of deer.  An intense fragrance perfumes the air, but all the roses in the world can't conceal the sickly-sweet stench of rotting meat that underlies it."],"exits":[{"to":35,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":34,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":37,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":37,"x":260,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Wild Rose Thicket","descriptions":["Pale pink roses blossom against thorny green leaves, growing in profusion in the dense thicket.  The trail twists and turns, following the hoofprints of countless generations of deer.  An intense fragrance perfumes the air, but all the roses in the world can't conceal the sickly-sweet stench of rotting meat that underlies it."],"exits":[{"to":36,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":39,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":38,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":38,"x":240,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Wild Rose Thicket","descriptions":["Pale pink roses blossom against thorny green leaves, growing in profusion in the dense thicket.  The trail twists and turns, following the hoofprints of countless generations of deer.  An intense fragrance perfumes the air, but all the roses in the world can't conceal the sickly-sweet stench of rotting meat that underlies it."],"exits":[{"to":37,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":39,"x":240,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Wild Rose Thicket","descriptions":["Pale pink roses blossom against thorny green leaves, growing in profusion in the dense thicket.  The trail twists and turns, following the hoofprints of countless generations of deer.  An intense fragrance perfumes the air, but all the roses in the world can't conceal the sickly-sweet stench of rotting meat that underlies it."],"exits":[{"to":41,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":37,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":40,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":40,"x":220,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Wild Rose Thicket","descriptions":["Pale pink roses blossom against thorny green leaves, growing in profusion in the dense thicket.  The trail twists and turns, following the hoofprints of countless generations of deer.  An intense fragrance perfumes the air, but all the roses in the world can't conceal the sickly-sweet stench of rotting meat that underlies it."],"exits":[{"to":39,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":41,"x":240,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Wild Rose Thicket","descriptions":["Pale pink roses blossom against thorny green leaves, growing in profusion in the dense thicket.  The trail twists and turns, following the hoofprints of countless generations of deer.  An intense fragrance perfumes the air, but all the roses in the world can't conceal the sickly-sweet stench of rotting meat that underlies it."],"exits":[{"to":29,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":42,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":39,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":42,"x":260,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Wild Rose Thicket","descriptions":["Pale pink roses blossom against thorny green leaves, growing in profusion in the dense thicket.  The trail twists and turns, following the hoofprints of countless generations of deer.  An intense fragrance perfumes the air, but all the roses in the world can't conceal the sickly-sweet stench of rotting meat that underlies it."],"exits":[{"to":41,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":43,"x":380,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["For the most part, the forest is painted in shades of grey on grey, from the dull charcoal bark of the mistwood trees to the pale, almost white lichens that cover fallen logs.  Occasional splashes of color break the monotone palate -- vivid scarlet leaves on a dark wyrdwood tree, or deep purple berries on a chokeweed bush.  The air is redolent with the smell of decaying leaves and rotting wood mingled with the faint sweet scent of blood."],"exits":[{"to":46,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":45,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":44,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":47,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":35,"exit":"go","move":"go thicket"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":44,"x":400,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["Musty leaves slip and slide underfoot, made slick by rain and slow decomposition.  Falling in graceful green veils, maiden's tresses drape over the branches to catch at the limbs of passersby."],"exits":[{"to":45,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":43,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":46,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":45,"x":400,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["Spiky stalks jut up from clusters of ferns that thrive in the depths of the forest, catching at skin and clothing.  The shadows of night are filled with the rustle of unseen footsteps making their way through the darkness.","Spiky cinnamon-brown stalks jut up from clusters of ferns that thrive in the shadows of the forest.  Here and there, a deep maroon trillium raises its face to the dim light of the sun."],"exits":[{"to":58,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":48,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":44,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":43,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":46,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":56,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":46,"x":380,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["A pockmarked boulder glitters with tiny garnet chips half hidden beneath flaky grey-green lichen.  Vivid moss clings to the northern side of the rock, smoothing the bumpy surface with a carpet of sharply scented greenery."],"exits":[{"to":56,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":58,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":45,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":44,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":43,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":47,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":47,"x":360,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["Dull red needles form a dense mat around the base of a pine tree, one of the few left in the forest.  For the most part, the quick growing conifers have been supplanted by the slower-growing grey mistwood so highly prized by lumbermen."],"exits":[{"to":56,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":46,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":43,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":48,"x":420,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["The forest crowds up against the base of a tall cliff to the east.  Angling out to loom over the huddled forest below, the sandstone surface looks almost impossible to climb.  High overhead, an owl circles as it hunts.","The forest crowds up against the base of a tall cliff to the east.  Angling out to loom over the huddled forest below, the sandstone surface looks almost impossible to climb.  High overhead, a raptor circles as it hunts."],"exits":[{"to":49,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":45,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":58,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":57,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":90,"exit":"climb","move":"climb cliff"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":49,"x":420,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["Moisture trickles down the face of a sandstone cliff, gathering in a shallow pool at the base.  Year after year, such trickles wear away at the smooth surface, leaving behind striated chimneys carved out of the surrounding rock."],"exits":[{"to":48,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":58,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":57,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":50,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":90,"exit":"climb","move":"climb chimney"}],"color":"#008000","aliases":["RTT18","RT-MF-LB"]},
  {"id":50,"x":400,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["Leaves whisper in the wind, twisting to reveal their red-veined undersides.  Quiet and peaceful, the serenity is belied by scraps of blood-stained fur caught on the rough bark of a tree trunk and the marks of claws in the damp loam of the forest floor."],"exits":[{"to":51,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":49,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":57,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":54,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":52,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000","aliases":["RTT17","RT-MF-MFG"]},
  {"id":51,"x":400,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["Bits of fur and broken bones litter the ground at the base of a tree, evidently the perch of an owl or some other bird of prey.  Overhanging branches sport a pale green fall of maiden's tresses that block your view of the upper reaches of the tree."],"exits":[{"to":50,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":54,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":52,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":52,"x":380,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["Scattered feathers shift fitfully in the breeze, all that remains of some hapless bird.  The trees grow close together, blocking the faint light that might be shed by the moons.  Shelf lichens cling to tree trunks, glowing with a faint phosphorescence.","Scattered feathers shift fitfully in the breeze, all that remains of some hapless bird.  The trees grow close together, leaving the forest floor shrouded in a perpetual twilight.  Shelf lichens cling to tree trunks, thriving in the damp climate."],"exits":[{"to":51,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":50,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":54,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":53,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":53,"x":360,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["The trail twists around, crossing and recrossing its path in an aimless meander.  A low buzzing sound draws your attention to a papery grey hornet's nest in the branches of a mistwood tree, fortunately out of reach."],"exits":[{"to":52,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":54,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":120,"exit":"go","move":"go embankment"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":54,"x":380,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["Patches of bark litter the forest floor, fallen from a dead tree across the path.  The exposed wood is riddled with tiny holes left by insects and larger holes left by the birds that prey upon them.  Despite the damage done by animals, the wood has aged to a lovely shade of silver-grey with dusky green veins."],"exits":[{"to":52,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":51,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":50,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":57,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":55,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":53,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":55,"x":360,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["A fox darts beneath a mistwood tree, disappearing into a tangle of thick roots.  Shadowed by the overhanging boughs, it's hard to see whether it went to earth in its den or lurks there, unseen."],"exits":[{"to":54,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":56,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":56,"x":380,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["Leaves rustle in counterpoint to a melodic twittering and chirping, a near-constant concert that falls silent from time to time as some threat is detected, only to begin again.  The birds themselves remain unseen, hidden by the dense foliage."],"exits":[{"to":57,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":58,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":45,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":46,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":47,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":55,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":57,"x":400,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["Past years' leaves lie crumpled and brown beneath the sheltering branches of the mistwood trees.  Every footstep and shift in position evokes a dry crackling noise as the fragile remains crumple underfoot."],"exits":[{"to":50,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":49,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":48,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":56,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":54,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":58,"x":400,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Deer Trail","descriptions":["Fireflies flicker in the darkness beneath the forest canopy, briefly illuminating a few shy lady's slipper orchids, or reflecting against the yellow eyes of a marauding raccoon as it trundles through the shrubbery.","Pale yellow against the forest floor, a few shy lady's slipper orchids sway in a slight breeze.  Overhead, squirrels leap from branch to branch with gleeful abandon as they go about their search for seeds and nuts to tide them over the winter months."],"exits":[{"to":49,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":48,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":45,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":46,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":56,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":59,"x":160,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Ruined Village, Inside the Gate","descriptions":["The village palisade, trimmed saplings bound together with rope and rusted iron bands, offers little protection against invaders.  From the looks of the shells of houses that residents once called their homes, there is little to attract bandits to prey upon the town.  Broken pottery, offal and other, less appealing substances line the sides of the dirt street, turning the packed earth into a reeking mud that clings to clothing and skin."],"exits":[{"to":67,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":60,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":68,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":66,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":33,"exit":"go","move":"go village gate"}]},
  {"id":60,"x":160,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Ruined Village, Stable","descriptions":["Built up against the palisade wall, the stable seems to have survived the destruction almost intact.  No glass remains in the structure's windows, but the split-shingled roof, while scorched from fire, displays little other damage.  The village well stands nearby, a broken bucket overturned beside it."],"exits":[{"to":59,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":61,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":62,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":68,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":66,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":86,"exit":"go","move":"go stable"}]},
  {"id":61,"x":160,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Ruined Village, Small Store","descriptions":["In the midst of the burnt-out cottages and broken fences, a sign still sways outside the doorway of what was once a small store.  The sturdy construction has left the building mostly intact, though its thatched roof, like all the houses in the town, has long since blown away."],"exits":[{"to":60,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":62,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":68,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":85,"exit":"go","move":"go small store"}]},
  {"id":62,"x":140,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Ruined Village, Blacksmith's Anvil","descriptions":["Streaked with rust, an anvil stands beneath a lightning-blasted tree.  Iron and steel bars lie in a tumbled haystack effect, melded together by the metal's oxidation to form a madman's sculpture.  Nearby houses are in no better shape, missing their roofs, their doors broken down and shutters swaying aimlessly in the breeze."],"exits":[{"to":68,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":60,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":61,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":64,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":63,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":65,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":84,"exit":"go","move":"go ruined house"}],"aliases":["House"]},
  {"id":63,"x":120,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Ruined Village, Manor House","descriptions":["Stone walls survive, but the thatched roof has long since blown away on the largest house still standing in the village.  Broken shutters surround the unglazed diamond-paned windows, still marred by black soot from the destruction of the village itself."],"exits":[{"to":65,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":68,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":62,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":64,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":69,"exit":"go","move":"go manor house"}]},
  {"id":64,"x":120,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Ruined Village, Granaries","descriptions":["Round wooden silos once stored grain for villagers.  Now the boards bow out as the wheat or barley held within swells from exposure to moisture, and a heady scent of fermentation fills the air."],"exits":[{"to":63,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":62,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}]},
  {"id":65,"x":120,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Ruined Village, Outside a Chapel","descriptions":["Fragments of colored glass litter the grass outside a small stone chapel.  Once a center for worship and a meeting place for the town, the building is now just a ruin towering over the tumbled-down cottages.  Splintered pews litter the small graveyard beside it, evidently used to knock down the markers on the graves."],"exits":[{"to":66,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":68,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":62,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":63,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":88,"exit":"go","move":"go chapel"}]},
  {"id":66,"x":140,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Ruined Village, Open Hearth","descriptions":["At one time, this must have been the site of a more conventional village, for a chimney and fireplace stand a lonely vigil amidst the ruins of a burnt-out house.  Rude wooden benches, little more than split logs, offer seating for residents to gather around what is now used as a communal cookfire.  A rusty cauldron swings from an iron hook over the sullenly burning logs in the hearth."],"exits":[{"to":67,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":59,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":60,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":68,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":65,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":67,"x":160,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Ruined Village, Near a Shanty","descriptions":["Old doors and close-growing saplings form the walls of one nearby shanty.  The trees themselves, still solidly rooted in the ground, are long-since dead from the noxious condition of the soil, but some enterprising resident has threaded willow withies between the trunks to form a rude shelter."],"exits":[{"to":59,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":66,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":89,"exit":"go","move":"go crude shanty"}]},
  {"id":68,"x":140,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Ruined Village, Common","descriptions":["Splintered stiles sag from weathered fence posts surrounding a muddy common, no longer a barrier to the passage of people or animals.  The canted remains of a small hut sway precariously in the breeze, perhaps once a manger for the animals that grazed here."],"exits":[{"to":66,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":59,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":60,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":61,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":62,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":63,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":65,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":87,"exit":"go","move":"go small hut"}]},
  {"id":69,"x":20,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Great Hall","descriptions":["Long oak trestle tables with matching benches line the walls, ready to be pulled out for the manor's evening meal.  Or so the hall was used in the days before the town's destruction.  Now, sticky with filth and spilled ale, the tables are piled high with straw to form rude beds for the invaders.  The rushes that cover the floor give off a sour smelling stench of mildew, mold and worse."],"exits":[{"to":71,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":70,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":73,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":63,"exit":"go","move":"go splintered door"},{"to":75,"exit":"climb","move":"climb curving staircase"}],"aliases":["Manor"]},
  {"id":70,"x":20,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Armory","descriptions":["Empty wooden racks once held swords and crossbows.  A barrel, half-filled with coarse black sand, would have been used to polish chainmail, removing the rust as a man at arms sweated to roll the barrel back and forth.  Now, the room holds naught but a few broken arrows and some bowstrings wrapped in oiled paper in a storage bin."],"exits":[{"to":69,"exit":"north","move":"north"}]},
  {"id":71,"x":20,"y":-110,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Kitchen","descriptions":["No fires burn in the great hearths at either end of the kitchen.  Now, they hold only cold ashes and the bitter memories of the once-thriving population that resided here.  Thick trestle tables are littered with broken pottery, some upturned against the wall and used as target practice, to judge by the splintered scars and broken arrowheads lodged within.  The flagstone floor is marred by sticky brown stains."],"exits":[{"to":72,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":69,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":74,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":72,"x":20,"y":-130,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Buttery","descriptions":["Stove-in barrels and the stale smell of ale fill the buttery.  Once used by the hall as a storage room for drinks, little remains but broken bottles and shards of earthenware tankards."],"exits":[{"to":71,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":73,"x":0,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Solar","descriptions":["A broken loom, still half threaded, stands near the long windows that overlook the orchard at the back of the manor.  Although frayed and tattered, the pattern of the unfinished tapestry is still visible beneath the accumulated dirt and cobwebs."],"exits":[{"to":69,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":74,"x":0,"y":-110,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Pantry","descriptions":["Rodent bones have been heaped in a pile in the corner of the pantry.  Marble shelves line the walls, so chipped and tilted as to be unusable.  Wooden barrels hold spoiled remains of wheat and oats, and an unbroken earthenware crock gives off a stench of rancid oil."],"exits":[{"to":71,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":75,"x":-20,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Hallway","descriptions":["The hall runs along the outer wall of the manor, lit only by narrow slit-like windows known as arrow loops.  Finely woven clothing, the expensive fabrics little more than tatters, litters the floor."],"exits":[{"to":78,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":77,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":76,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":69,"exit":"climb","move":"climb curving staircase"}]},
  {"id":76,"x":-40,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Master Bedroom","descriptions":["Shredded hangings sway from the posts of the carved mahogany bed like dull grey ghosts of the past.  Moths have been at the draperies, leaving behind cobweb-strewn fabric that more closely resembles fuzzy lace than the original rich green velvet.  Pale brown feathers drift in the air, swept up from holes in the mattress ticking by the wind.  An iron-banded chest at the foot of the bed lies open and empty."],"exits":[{"to":75,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":77,"x":-20,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, White Bedroom","descriptions":["Chill white walls and dingy white damask drapes make the cherrywood bed seem to glow a deep, rich red color despite the lack of polish and exposure to the elements.  The mattress is missing -- dragged off to use for bedding elsewhere or simply eaten by rodents.  Nothing else remains in the room but dust and dirt."],"exits":[{"to":75,"exit":"north","move":"north"}]},
  {"id":78,"x":-20,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Hallway","descriptions":["The hall runs along the outer wall of the manor, lit only by narrow slit-like windows known as arrow loops.  Empty torch rings frame the doors along the inner wall, and a dimly lit staircase leads up to the attics."],"exits":[{"to":79,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":75,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":80,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":81,"exit":"climb","move":"climb staircase"}]},
  {"id":79,"x":-20,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Nursery","descriptions":["An overturned cot lies sprawled in the ashes of the fireplace, seared and crackled by heat.  Nearby, two small cradles hold scattered bones amidst the linen bedding.  Less damage was done here than in the other rooms of the manor -- the dressers remain standing, and the flames were confined to the fireplace itself.  Dirt has settled into the corners, veiled by a year or more of spider webs, and choking clouds of dust rise up with each movement."],"exits":[{"to":78,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":80,"x":-40,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Blue Bedroom","descriptions":["Torn strips of sapphire-blue wallpaper sag to the floor, revealing the whitewashed walls behind it.  A dark blue braided rug is the only furnishing in this empty bedroom."],"exits":[{"to":78,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":81,"x":-40,"y":-110,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Attics","descriptions":["The roof is missing, burnt by the fires which ravaged the village or simply lost to time and weather, leaving the attics open to the sky.  Dark rafters tower overhead, and a narrow staircase leads down to the lower floors."],"exits":[{"to":82,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":83,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":78,"exit":"climb","move":"climb staircase"}]},
  {"id":82,"x":-40,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Storeroom","descriptions":["Toppled trunks, their sides bashed in, are scattered across the floor of the storeroom.  Open to the weather, the wood has swollen and dried, cracking a little more with each cycle until jagged splinters offer a hazard to anyone lacking sturdy boots."],"exits":[{"to":81,"exit":"north","move":"north"}]},
  {"id":83,"x":-60,"y":-110,"z":0,"title":"Manor House, Servant's Quarters","descriptions":["Wind and rain have swept the floorboards bare, leaving behind little more than warped and weathered wood.  Wooden rings on iron bars between the rafters are all that remain of the curtains used to divide the large room into smaller cubbies for the servants who worked from dawn to long past dark to keep the manor house running."],"exits":[{"to":81,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":84,"x":140,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"A Ruined House","descriptions":["Scraps of wood litter the floor, shredded by sharp teeth and stained dark by blood.  Once upon a time, this might have been some housewife's home.  The splintered table is now laid with a haphazard arrangement of bones in some lunatic's version of a place setting.  Rats browse in the dirty straw pallets along the walls, gnawing on discarded grain or meat.  The patchy remains of the thatched roof do little to keep out the weather."],"exits":[{"to":62,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["House"]},
  {"id":85,"x":160,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Small Store","descriptions":["Withered apples, onions and potatoes spill from bushel baskets, pillowing the bolts of cloth and tools fallen from shelves lining the walls.  Now, those shelves are splintered by the marks of axes or swords, and the wooden counter opposite the doorway is caked with years of accumulated dust and dirt."],"exits":[{"to":61,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":155,"exit":"climb","move":"objsearch rubble climb stairway"}],"aliases":["Store"]},
  {"id":86,"x":170,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Ruined Village, Inside a Stable","descriptions":["Gnawed bones litter the stable floor, mute testimony to the fate of the animals that once lived here.  Piles of mildewed hay lie tumbled about in careless abandon, now populated only by fleas and other vermin."],"exits":[{"to":60,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["Stable"]},
  {"id":87,"x":120,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Inside a Small Hut","descriptions":["A wooden bin hangs on the back wall of this three-sided hut.  The front is open to the common, allowing animals easy access to shelter during the rain.  Lack of maintenance and years of weather damage have left the hut swaying in the least breeze, and every gust of wind brings with it the chance of total collapse."],"exits":[{"to":68,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["Hut"]},
  {"id":88,"x":120,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Ruined Village, In the Chapel","descriptions":["Soot streaks the walls and floors, radiating out from the heat-seared marks left by a bonfire.  The invaders must have burned the chapel's pews and woodwork, leaving behind this bare stone building furnished with lice-ridden straw pallets covered by mounds of fraying woolen blankets and half-tanned furs."],"exits":[{"to":65,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["Chapel"]},
  {"id":89,"x":170,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"A Crude Shanty","descriptions":["Dark and dismal, the ground in this hovel smells of mold and mildew, reminiscent of a grave.  The owner has never bothered cutting windows, and the door consists of nothing more than a blanket poked between some of the tree branches."],"exits":[{"to":67,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["Shanty"]},
  {"id":90,"x":520,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Sandstone Cliff","descriptions":["A narrow ledge juts out from the rocky face of the cliff, allowing one to examine the beauty of the forest below.  A few wispy tufts of grass cling desperately to the edge, their strands swaying gently in a passing wind.  Two small daisies, their stems intertwined, sit in the center of one particular tuft.  The way down is either over the smooth cliff face or a nearby chimney which has formed over the long years."],"exits":[{"to":92,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":91,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":49,"exit":"climb","move":"climb chimney"},{"to":93,"exit":"climb","move":"climb handhold"},{"to":48,"exit":"climb","move":"climb cliff"}],"aliases":["forest gryphons","gryphons"]},
  {"id":91,"x":560,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Gryphon Eyrie, Rookery","descriptions":["Phosphorescent algae cast a dim light over this cavern.  Part of a larger nest, the walls and floor have been painstakingly insulated with a layer of branches and leaves.  Near the back of the cavern lay a large number of eggs, waiting to hatch.  The eggs are protected from intruders by a wide chasm that runs through the center of the cavern.  A rather large, surly looking gryphon lies protectively near the eggs, appearing unwilling to move for an intruder on this side of the chasm.","Phosphorescent algae cast a dim light over this cavern.  Part of a larger nest, the walls and floor have been painstakingly insulated with a layer of branches and leaves.  Near the back of the cavern lay a large number of eggs, waiting to hatch.  The eggs are protected from intruders by a wide chasm that runs through the center of the cavern."],"exits":[{"to":92,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":90,"exit":"out","move":"out"}]},
  {"id":92,"x":540,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Gryphon Eyrie, Nest","descriptions":["A large nest has been built, deep in the cave.  Constructed of branches, bones, and leaves, the nest is filled with layers of soft feathers.  An occasional fragment of thick shell is evidence that whatever built the nest belongs to a large species.  The partially eaten scraps of meat indicate that the species might not welcome visitors."],"exits":[{"to":91,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":90,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":0,"exit":"climb","move":"climb slope"}]},
  {"id":93,"x":520,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Sandstone Cliff","descriptions":["A deep recess in the face of the cliff gives travelers bit of freedom to move about.  A huge oak tree on one side of the depression looks slightly lopsided, having grown so close to the face of the cliff that it is stunted on that side.  The lower limbs of the tree grow close to the ground, granting access to some of the higher limbs.  The tree shades the recess, and nearly hides a wide crack at the back.  Handholds have been carved into the face of the cliff, leading down."],"exits":[{"to":94,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":90,"exit":"climb","move":"climb handhold"},{"to":116,"exit":"go","move":"go crack"}],"aliases":["young forest gryphons","young gryphons"]},
  {"id":94,"x":520,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Sandstone Cliff, Oak Limb","descriptions":["This broad limb stretches forth from the trunk of the tree, thick enough to support a good deal of weight.  The view reveals that this limb is approximately half way between a ledge below and the top of the cliff above.  The closest limbs within reach are those that lead down towards the narrow ledge.  The only branches leading upwards are too far for even the tallest Gor'Tog, so that one cannot climb in that direction.  A wide hole in the side of the trunk looks broad enough to squeeze through."],"exits":[{"to":95,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":93,"exit":"down","move":"down"}],"aliases":["mature forest gryphons","mature gryphons"]},
  {"id":95,"x":540,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Sandstone Cliff, Inside the Oak","descriptions":["The hollow within the tree is larger than would appear from the outside.  It extends upwards where little bits of sky are visible through an open knothole.  The walls are smooth, with the exception of the edges around a hole leading outwards at ground level, making it impossible to climb them.  Fortunately, some thoughtful traveler left a rope, allowing others to climb up to the knothole."],"exits":[{"to":94,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":96,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rope"}]},
  {"id":96,"x":540,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Cliff","descriptions":["Mistwood trees press in around the edge of the cliff, a few clinging rather tenuously to the ground.  A stout rope has been tied to a nearby stump and leads through an open knothole in the side of an oak tree which begins somewhere below the edge of the cliff and towers up over it.  Older layers of leaves, nearly decomposed now, have been kicked up in various places by someone, or something.  A series of low limbs offers a route to the upper branches of one stout tree."],"exits":[{"to":107,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":110,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":109,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":95,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rope"},{"to":97,"exit":"climb","move":"climb limb"}]},
  {"id":97,"x":540,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Treetop","descriptions":["Broad, thick mistwood branches grow in a tangled mess and form a highway high over the forest floor.  Some branches do not lead anywhere, while others connect and form wooden bridges between trees.  The limbs of one tree lead down to a spot where it is possible to drop to the ground, though it might be difficult and could result in a fall."],"exits":[{"to":98,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":101,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":100,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":96,"exit":"climb","move":"climb limb"}]},
  {"id":98,"x":560,"y":-110,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Treetop","descriptions":["The branches overhead thin slightly, allowing a clear view of the sky above.  Below, dense thickets cover the leaf-strewn ground, possibly providing a bit of cushion for those who might fall.  Limbs form a spiraling staircase that provides a means to get down to the forest floor."],"exits":[{"to":99,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":101,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":97,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":99,"x":580,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Treetop","descriptions":["From your vantage point you can see a stone road below.  To the east, as the forest thins, the branches become less dense and tangled.  A series of blue rags, tied to branches, marks a route through the thinning forest canopy to the east.  The trunk of one tree is scratched on one side, as if it has been used frequently to climb between the ground and the treetops."],"exits":[{"to":103,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":102,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":100,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":101,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":98,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":100,"x":560,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Treetop","descriptions":["The trees grow close together, a jumbled mass of branches and trunks.  Moving about is a bit difficult, but not impossible.  The ground below is completely obscured by branches and the sky is only visible in fleeting glimpses.  Small scraps of tattered white cloth have been conveniently placed to mark routes where it is possible to travel.  An assortment of red cloths hangs from a set of branches that lead down to the forest floor."],"exits":[{"to":101,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":99,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":102,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":97,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":101,"x":560,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Treetop","descriptions":["Broad avenues of branches stretch out in every direction, high above the ground.  Most of the branches look sturdy enough to support a good deal of weight, while others look like they could snap under the slightest pressure.  One branch has broken, and its fallen half now lies dead on the forest floor.  A series of stout limbs forms a natural ladder to the ground below."],"exits":[{"to":98,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":99,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":102,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":100,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":97,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":102,"x":580,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Treetop","descriptions":["The branches arch over the ground, giving one a view of a small clearing below where a pit has been dug.  The trees seem to shy away from the pit, none daring to grow too close to its edge.  One tree has fallen over, providing a steep ramp to the ground below."],"exits":[{"to":103,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":104,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":100,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":99,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":103,"x":600,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Treetop","descriptions":["Branches form a thick canopy, obscuring the forest floor except for faint glimpses of the remains of a stone road.  The thicker, sturdier branches form a highway that echoes the path of the stone road.  One especially large mistwood tree along the path looks like a somewhat passable, if awkward and difficult way to climb down to the ground."],"exits":[{"to":106,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":104,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":102,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":99,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":104,"x":600,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Treetop","descriptions":["The trees begin to disperse noticeably to the east.  The trees are thinner than are those to the west, clumping together in small groves.  The smaller bodies are close enough together that passage between each cluster of trees is possible.  The sturdy limbs of the mistwood trees allow one with a good bit of skill or perhaps luck to climb down to the ground."],"exits":[{"to":106,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":105,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":102,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":103,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":105,"x":620,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Treetop","descriptions":["The trees in this part of the forest are clustered together in sparsely populated groves.  Passage is difficult due to the wide distance between clusters of trees.  A chain of trees echoes a stone road below and allows passage to the west and northeast.  One of the taller mistwood trees offers a route down to the ground."],"exits":[{"to":106,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":104,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":106,"x":620,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Treetop","descriptions":["At the edge of the forest the trees are few and far between, while to the west the growth thickens.  To the east a stone road climbs partway up a rock-strewn hill.  A series of connecting branches form a broad avenue high in the treetop canopy.  A mistwood tree at the extreme edge of the forest offers a way down to the road for those foolhardy or skilled enough."],"exits":[{"to":105,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":104,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":103,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":107,"x":560,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Among the Trees","descriptions":["Dense clusters of brush and scrub mark this part of the forest.  Game trails run from southerly bearings and begin to scatter in a large number of directions heading north.  The northern trails disappear beneath the local chaparral, making them impossible to follow.  The bones of some small animal, partially hidden at the edge of a bush, have been gathered into a pile and the skull placed on top.  The limbs of one tree almost form a spiraling staircase as they circle upwards to the top of the tree."],"exits":[{"to":108,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":110,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":96,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":108,"x":580,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Among the Trees","descriptions":["A weathered pile of rocks has been stacked rather carefully, marking the boundary between a game trail leading west and a stone road that winds through the forest to the east.  Off the beaten trail the ground is thick with foliage, carpeting it in a fresh layer of green leaves.  The rough bark of one mistwood tree makes natural places to grip when scaling the trunk, creating a possible place to climb."],"exits":[{"to":112,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":111,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":109,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":110,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":107,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":109,"x":560,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Among the Trees","descriptions":["The ground is thick with foliage fallen from the trees.  The trees seem to huddle together, forming a thick canopy and almost completely blocking the sky above.  A narrow path winds through the trees, running north and angling sharply east, with the occasional gnarled root or branch nearly blocking the way.  The densely packed trees form a highway of branches overhead with access from some of the limbs closer to the ground."],"exits":[{"to":110,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":108,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":111,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":96,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":110,"x":560,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Among the Trees","descriptions":["The forest is quiet, broken only by the sound of the occasional bird chirp, which is then quickly silenced.  The trees have been badly damaged, with what would appear to be claw marks on almost every tree in the immediate vicinity.  Game trails stretch in the four cardinal directions, dodging between the trees.  Low limbs on one tree look particularly stout and good for climbing."],"exits":[{"to":107,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":108,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":111,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":109,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":96,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":111,"x":580,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Pit","descriptions":["A small clearing has formed in the midst of the dense trees.  The trees grow a respectable distance away from a large pit that has been dug in the middle of the clearing.  The sides of the pit are smooth, which would have made escape impossible if one of the walls had not collapsed into a large pile of rubble, partially filling the pit.  One tree has fallen over onto another so that it leans at an angle perfect for scaling to some of the higher branches."],"exits":[{"to":112,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":113,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":109,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":108,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":112,"x":600,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Under the Canopy","descriptions":["The woods press in on the road oppressively, forming a thick canopy overhead.  A small portion of the road is virtually untouched by the ravages of time, as the stones are still tightly fitted together.  The superb construction demonstrates the care and hard work that the laborers put into the road's assembly.  Weeds and grasses have grown between most of the stones that once formed the road."],"exits":[{"to":114,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":113,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":111,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":108,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":113,"x":600,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Under the Canopy","descriptions":["The trees clump together in groves, densely packed, but with visible differences from what can be seen to the west.  Fallen leaves nearly cover a pile of stones off to one side of the road.  At the base of the pile one of the rocks looks as if it had been inscribed, though the words are too faded to make out."],"exits":[{"to":114,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":115,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":111,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":112,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":114,"x":620,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Forest's Edge","descriptions":["The trees are fewer and far between towards the edge of the forest.  Smaller varieties of plant life flourish with little competition from the larger trees.  The undergrowth continues out past the last of the trees and a short ways up the slope of a rocky hill.  A mistwood tree near the road offers a way up into the canopy."],"exits":[{"to":115,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":113,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":112,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":115,"x":620,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Forest's Edge","descriptions":["Thick growths of underbrush rule this part of the forest.  Interspersed between the thickets are a few sparse clusters of mistwood trees.  A small brook gurgles as it meanders through the forest and crosses the path of the road.  Alongside the brook grows a single lilac, a stranger among giants."],"exits":[{"to":114,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":113,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":116,"x":540,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Gryphon Eyrie, Entrance","descriptions":["Bones and feathers litter the floor near a wide crack in the wall leading out.  A few large, black stains mar the ground amongst the debris.  The air is cool, though stagnant, and carries muffled cries from elsewhere in the cave."],"exits":[{"to":117,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":118,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":119,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":93,"exit":"go","move":"go crack"}]},
  {"id":117,"x":560,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Gryphon Eyrie, Den","descriptions":["The north wall of this tunnel has collapsed, blocking all passage in that direction.  Part of the tunnel shows signs of digging and a few of the larger rocks bear the scars from the scratching of claws.  The air is moist and cool, helping to foster a community of phosphorescent algae which clings to the east wall."],"exits":[{"to":118,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":119,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":116,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":118,"x":580,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Gryphon Eyrie, Den","descriptions":["A steady trickling sound emanates from a miniature waterfall in one wall.  The waterfall feeds a crystal clear pool which empties into a narrow rivulet.  The rivulet carries the water into a low tunnel in the opposite wall and disappears.  Through the crystalline waters you can see phosphorescent algae growing in the bottom of the pool, glowing softly."],"exits":[{"to":119,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":116,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":117,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":119,"x":560,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Gryphon Eyrie, Den","descriptions":["Small, downy feathers are scattered about on the floor.  A rocky slope leads downward and farther into the cave, where shrill cries issue forth.  The ground is heavily pitted and scratched where numerous claws have dug into the rock.  The carcass of some poor beast lies on the floor, its bones nearly picked clean."],"exits":[{"to":117,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":118,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":116,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":92,"exit":"climb","move":"climb slope"}]},
  {"id":120,"x":360,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Gyfford's Bridge, Southeast Embankment","descriptions":["The forest has been cleared away from the approach of this bridge, allowing room for a wide abutment that supports an embankment that arcs over the ravine in the Mistwood Forest floor.  Granite and quartzite are layered in a cobblestone pattern, leading upward to a deck supported entirely from the stone construction on each side."],"exits":[{"to":154,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":53,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":121,"x":360,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, North of a Ravine","descriptions":["A steep-sided ravine breaches the forest floor, leaving a wide gash spanned by a stone bridge.  The freshly cut stones of the construction show little sign of weathering or wear, some still displaying mason's marks or chisel scrapes.  A massive embankment leads the way across.","A steep-sided ravine breaches the forest floor, leaving a wide gash spanned by a pair of ropes tied to trees on either side.  It's hard to dignify the arrangement by calling it a bridge, but it looks like the only way across."],"exits":[{"to":153,"exit":"go","move":"go embankment"},{"to":123,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":122,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":138,"exit":"climb","move":"objsearch ravine climb crack"}]},
  {"id":122,"x":340,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Clearing","descriptions":["Packed earth trails, wide enough for a wagon, wind through the trees and stumps of the forest.  A charcoal burner's hut stands in a small clearing, surrounded by smoking mounds of earth that cover stacks of slowly smoldering wood."],"exits":[{"to":121,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":123,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":124,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":123,"x":320,"y":-70,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Trail","descriptions":["A winding ravine blocks travel to the south.  There's no way to cross at this point, but you can see a pair of ropes spanning the divide a bit further east.  The trees are sparse near the edge of the cliff, and the ground underfoot is crumbling in places."],"exits":[{"to":124,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":122,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":121,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":124,"x":320,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Trail","descriptions":["Grey barked mistwood trees line the trail, their broad leaves cupped to cradle the dew.  The moons, filtered by overhanging branches and dense foliage, cast more shadows than illumination, an effect that is only heightened by the faint, pallid glow of phosphorescent mosses clinging to the tree trunks.  From time to time, a hunting cat gives off a hoarse yowl of frustration, presumably to curse the escape of its prey.","Grey barked mistwood trees shade the trail, filtering the light to a pale shade of green.  The air is cool on even the hottest summer days as the furled leaves release a faint mist that gives the tree its name."],"exits":[{"to":122,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":123,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":125,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":125,"x":300,"y":-110,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Trail","descriptions":["The ground underfoot is soft with layer upon layer of decaying leaves.  A fine haze fills the air, reflecting every beam of moonlight that manages to penetrate the forest canopy.","The ground underfoot is soft with layer upon layer of decaying leaves.  A fine haze fills the air, reflecting every beam of sunlight that manages to penetrate the forest canopy."],"exits":[{"to":124,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":126,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":126,"x":280,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Trail","descriptions":["Tall spikes of pale purple flowers sway above the broad leaves of hosta growing in the shade of the forest.  Grey-barked mistwood trees grow close together, broken here and there by clumps of river birch or oak."],"exits":[{"to":125,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":127,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":127,"x":260,"y":-110,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Trail","descriptions":["Motes of dust dance in beams of moonlight that filter through the tree branches.  The trail narrows as it passes deeper into the forest.  Though the chitter of birds may fade with the setting sun, the forest is never silent, as even the leaves whisper against one another in the wind.","Motes of dust dance in stray beams of sunlight that flicker through the tree branches.  The trail narrows as it passes deeper into the forest.  Though the chitter of birds may fade at your approach, the forest is never silent, as even the leaves whisper against one another in the wind."],"exits":[{"to":126,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":128,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":128,"x":240,"y":-110,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Forest's Edge","descriptions":["An occasional dark grey-barked mistwood tree jostles for space amidst the faster-growing birch and pine here on the edge of the forest.  The sharp needles and gum-laden branches of the pines tend to catch at the hair and clothing of those passing beneath the trees, as if some wood sprite did try to cling to those who travel through her domain."],"exits":[{"to":127,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":129,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":129,"x":220,"y":-90,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, Forest's Edge","descriptions":["Cloaked in the forest's pale twilight world of greenery, you can see the brighter greens and golds of the fields to the north and the dark browns and greys of the forest to the east.  The road grows rougher as it enters the forest, rutted and churned by passing wagons and lack of maintenance."],"exits":[{"to":130,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":128,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":130,"x":220,"y":-130,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["Wide swathes of oats and wheat, their colors faded in the night, ripen in fields on either side of the road.  A split-log fence prevents cattle from straying into the crops.  To the south, trees grow thickly together as the road enters the shadows of the Mistwood Forest.","Wide swathes of oats and wheat ripen beneath the sun's gentle rays in fields on either side of the road.  A split-log fence prevents cattle from straying into the crops.  To the south, trees grow thickly together as the road enters the shadows of the Mistwood Forest."],"exits":[{"to":131,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":129,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":131,"x":240,"y":-130,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["A few small thatched-roof cottages cluster beside the road in a bucolic setting.  Assorted livestock move restlessly within a pen -- a bristle-maned grey donkey, a pair of oxen and a swaybacked nag with a shaggy coat.  The animals' legs are coated in mud or some other, less appealing substance."],"exits":[{"to":132,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":130,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":132,"x":260,"y":-150,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["A spring wells up from the ground beside the road, trickling down a rocky outcropping to pool in a stone basin.  Local residents rely on it for their animals and crops, as the overflow from the basin runs into a ditch used to irrigate surrounding fields."],"exits":[{"to":133,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":131,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":133,"x":260,"y":-170,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["Cattle lowing in a nearby pasture break the silence of the surrounding countryside.  Flowers and herbs bloom in small gardens between the houses that border the road.  Though quite similar in construction, each building each has some feature to distinguish it from its neighbor.  One house has fruit trees, another a pen for a pig, while yet another is home to a box-like shelter mounted atop a pole in front."],"exits":[{"to":132,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":134,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":134,"x":240,"y":-190,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["Rolling hills stretch out on either side of the road, covered with a thick mat of wild thyme and rosemary.  Tiny white and purple flowers dot the fragrant greenery."],"exits":[{"to":133,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":135,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":135,"x":220,"y":-170,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["A wooden tower at the crest of the hill offers a view of the surrounding countryside.  In the dry season, the Baron's foresters keep a careful watch for fires that could destroy the prosperous fields."],"exits":[{"to":136,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":134,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":136,"x":220,"y":-190,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest Road","descriptions":["To the south, the rolling hills give way to orchards and neatly tended fields.  The road to Mistwood Forest stretches out to the south and east, branching off from the main North Road that connects Therenborough with the village of Langenfirth."],"exits":[{"to":135,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":137,"exit":"go","move":"go road"}],"color":"#008000"},
  {"id":137,"x":220,"y":-210,"z":0,"title":"North Road, Farmlands","descriptions":["The surrounding, gracefully-sloping hillsides are thickly carpeted with juniper, thyme and rosemary that fill the air with a fresh herbal fragrance."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":0,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":136,"exit":"go","move":"go road"}],"aliases":["Therenborough","Langenfirth"],"linksTo":"Map40_Langenfirth_to_Therenborough.xml"},
  {"id":138,"x":420,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["Narrow cracks in the ravine wall offer an escape from the shadows of the canyon, though to judge by the amount of rubble littering the rocky floor, treacherous is probably the kindest way to describe the climb."],"exits":[{"to":146,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":145,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":139,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":121,"exit":"climb","move":"climb crack"}]},
  {"id":139,"x":400,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["A boulder juts up from the ravine floor to the south, blocking travel in that direction.  The walls of the ravine are shrouded in shadows, but there seems no easy way out from here."],"exits":[{"to":138,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":145,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":140,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":140,"x":380,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["Deep cracks in the canyon floor widen to the west, making further travel impossible.  Though the bottom is not visible, the sound of rushing water echoes up from the depths of the crevice."],"exits":[{"to":139,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":141,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":141,"x":400,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["Reflected moonlight shimmers against the water in a deep sink pit along the south side of the ravine.  Steep rock walls overhang the canyon floor, making it difficult to distinguish details of the surrounding area."],"exits":[{"to":145,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":144,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":143,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":142,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":140,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":142,"x":380,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["Broken rocks, fallen from the ravine walls, litter the ground with splintered shards.  Years of erosion have cut away at the south wall, leaving it to rise at a steep inward-leaning angle that even the most intrepid mountain goat could not navigate.  High overhead, two ropes cross the top of the ravine, far out of reach."],"exits":[{"to":141,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":143,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":143,"x":400,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["Shallow grooves worn by years of running water undulate across the floor of the ravine.  The depressions form catch-basins for rubble fallen from the rock walls, filling with gravel and other debris to make for hazardous footing.  Overhead, the south wall of the ravine leans in at an acute angle, making it impossible to climb."],"exits":[{"to":141,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":144,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":142,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":144,"x":420,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["A sink pit near the south wall is filled with ice-cold water that spills over the side of the ravine.  The trail skirts the obstacle, winding in a smooth arc through the rubble-strewn canyon."],"exits":[{"to":143,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":141,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":145,"x":420,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["Water ripples as wind skitters across a sink pit along the south wall, sending flickers of light dancing around the ravine.  High overhead, a pair of ropes span the top of the canyon, occasionally traversed by travelers, but more often providing a precarious perch for hawks hunting small rodents in the gorge."],"exits":[{"to":138,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":146,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":151,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":141,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":139,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":146,"x":440,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["Worn by years of falling water, the ravine wall exhibits gentle folds running from floor to rim.  The north wall rises nearly straight up, unlike the inward tilt of the southern wall.  While it doesn't seem possible to climb out at this point, perhaps it will be further down the ravine."],"exits":[{"to":147,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":152,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":145,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":138,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":147,"x":460,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["Dark boulders topped with a stone slab form a crude altar in the shadow of the ravine walls.  A hollow in the slab holds a bit of stagnant water, and a dried snake skin and a desiccated cardinal's wing with a few bedraggled feathers still clinging to it lie nearby."],"exits":[{"to":148,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":152,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":146,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#A6A3D9","aliases":["Zachriedek","Altar"]},
  {"id":148,"x":480,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["A rockfall blocks the ravine to the east, leaving behind shifting piles of shale too precarious to climb.  Green with mold and decay, a few bones are visible amidst the sharp-edged rubble."],"exits":[{"to":149,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":152,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":147,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":149,"x":460,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["High along the ravine's southern wall, a bird has built a large nest.  There's no way to get to it from here, however, and no sign of the occupant."],"exits":[{"to":152,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":148,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":150,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":151,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":150,"x":460,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["The ravine wall takes a sharp turn, forming a sheltered hollow less exposed to the wind.  Some previous traveler has evidently taken advantage of this, given the remains of a fire pit surrounded by a few comfortably curved stones."],"exits":[{"to":149,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":151,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":151,"x":440,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["Wind rushes through the canyon, ruffling the surface of the water in a nearby sink pit and catching at hair and clothing of travelers making their way through the gorge.  The high walls funnel the force to send it whipping remorselessly against any exposed skin."],"exits":[{"to":152,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":149,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":150,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":145,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":152,"x":460,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Mistwood Forest, In a Ravine","descriptions":["Shards of sharp-edged shale litter the floor of the ravine, a hazard to anyone foolish enough to go barefoot in the dim light.  From time to time, a few rocks bounce along the rocky surface as something moves in the shadows."],"exits":[{"to":147,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":148,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":149,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":151,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":146,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":153,"x":360,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Gyfford's Bridge, Northwest Embankment","descriptions":["Ascending the steep bank of the ravine across the Mistwood Forest floor, a terraced abutment of stone and mortar supports the cobblestone embankment of the northwest face of this bridge.  Layers of stone follow the gradient of the bridge to provide support, with visible color variation from the granite and quartzite used in its construction."],"exits":[{"to":121,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":154,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":154,"x":360,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Gyfford's Bridge, Deck","descriptions":["From atop the sturdy construction of the arching bridge, you can observe broken rocks scattered at the bottom of the ravine over a safety wall.  Wind whips through the narrow ravine.  Beneath you, quartzite and granite cobblestone provides a firm support in what would otherwise undoubtedly be a precarious position, a testament to engineering.  A plaque at the pinnacle of the arch marks the dedication of the bridge."],"exits":[{"to":153,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":120,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":155,"x":100,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Viggu's Lair, Tunnels","descriptions":["Once used for storage by the proprietors of the small shop above, the surrounding shelves now lay splintered and broken amid baskets of decayed stock.  Several rusted tools are strewn along the dirt floor including a shovel planted deep within the pile of soil next to a tunnel that slopes downward into the darkness."],"exits":[{"to":156,"exit":"down","move":"down"},{"to":85,"exit":"climb","move":"climb dusty stairway"}],"aliases":["Viggu's Lair"]},
  {"id":156,"x":90,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Viggu's Lair, Tunnels","descriptions":["Rough dirt walls expose stone and roots mingled within the soil along the dark passage which branches off in different directions from the juncture.  Crude reed torches are held by make-shift iron supports thrust into the crumbling walls, their flickering light disclosing deep ruts dug into the ground that vanish into the darkness of the tunnels beyond."],"exits":[{"to":160,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":157,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":155,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":157,"x":80,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Viggu's Lair, Tunnels","descriptions":["Crudely etched boulders are embedded along the rough walls of the dimly lit corridor.  Rusted manacles hang from chains above a slow trickle of water which bleeds downward from beyond a crack in the stone, pooling along the ground with an incessant drip."],"exits":[{"to":156,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":158,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":158,"x":70,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Viggu's Lair, Tunnels","descriptions":["Flickering light from the nearby torch casts long, wavering shadows from the thick, rotting planks that rest against the rough dirt walls.  Set into the northwest corner of the sharp bend is a large wooden door mounted within heavy beams, blocking further passage into the area."],"exits":[{"to":159,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":157,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":159,"x":90,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Viggu's Lair, Tunnels","descriptions":["Piles of dirt and rock clutter the ground from an overhead collapse along the bend of the crudely dug, dark tunnel.  Along one wall, several cracked wooden buckets are tossed beside rusted spades and pick axes, now covered in short mosses and spidery roots that creep from the ground."],"exits":[{"to":160,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":158,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":160,"x":100,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Viggu's Lair, Tunnels","descriptions":["Flickering light from a crude reed torch wavers across the rough dirt walls, revealing a collapsed tunnel to the east.  Appearing to crawl from the crushing rubble are partially exposed skeletal remains, the bony fingers embedded in the crumbled debris of the cave in."],"exits":[{"to":156,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":159,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":161,"x":100,"y":210,"z":0,"title":"Jantspyre River, Rapids","descriptions":["Swift moving currents batter against the rocks that jut out of the stream to leave them slick and smooth.  The lichen that clings to the boulders down-river is missing here, unable to survive the torrents of water that rage with relentless fury against all in its path."],"exits":[{"to":162,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":9,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}],"color":"#0000FF","aliases":["Rapids"]},
  {"id":162,"x":120,"y":210,"z":0,"title":"Jantspyre River, Rapids","descriptions":["No boat could possibly survive these rock-strewn rapids that strive to thrust you downstream.  Treacherous undercurrents tug at your feet, pressing you back against one of the massive boulders.  This is but a moment's respite, however, as the slick surface offers little for you to cling to, and the shifting gravel in the riverbed makes it hard to keep your feet."],"exits":[{"to":163,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":161,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":163,"x":140,"y":190,"z":0,"title":"Jantspyre River, Rapids","descriptions":["A sullen roar echoes off the river's rocky banks, almost deafening to hear.  Currents swirl and eddy in a vicious whirlpool that threatens to suck your body into oblivion, while clouds of mist obscure your view of all beyond an arm's distance."],"exits":[{"to":162,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":164,"exit":"east","move":"east"}],"color":"#0000FF"},
  {"id":164,"x":160,"y":190,"z":0,"title":"Jantspyre River, Cataract","descriptions":["A mist-coated basalt cliff rises overhead, blocking further travel up-river.  Boulders atop the cliff divide the cataract into five twisting threads that surge out in a glittering descent into the deeper water at the base of the falls.  Rainbows move in a mad dance of refracted light within the mist, chasing the spray for a moment, then darting back into the shelter of the rocks, only to break out anew in another location."],"exits":[{"to":163,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#0000FF","aliases":["Cataract"]},
  {"id":165,"x":-80,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Eastgate Road","descriptions":["Within the wooden palisade, work has begun on a stone curtain wall.  About six spans in width, it abuts the existing town wall, reinforcing the logs and providing a more secure defense for the residents.  Beginning at the stone arch around the portcullis, the new wall extends to the north and south about half the length of the existing lumber one."],"exits":[{"to":171,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":167,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":166,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"}],"aliases":["Eastgate Road","Gate"]},
  {"id":166,"x":-60,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Foregate Passage","descriptions":["A guard stands just within the iron-banded outer gates, checking travelers as they come through.  The high archway leading to the town is guarded by a massive iron portcullis, raised and lowered by a windlass someplace within.  Gaps between the logs roofing the foregate passage allow defenders to rain down rocks, hot oil or other, less appealing substances upon would-be intruders."],"exits":[{"to":165,"exit":"go","move":"go arch"},{"to":3,"exit":"go","move":"go gate"}]},
  {"id":167,"x":-80,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Eastgate Road","descriptions":["The pungent aroma and muffled neighs of horses mark the low building nearby as a stable, even without the horseshoe-shaped wooden sign hanging above the door.  Ostlers and grooms bustle about, some walking horses, others carrying buckets of water from a nearby well to fill the trough in front.  A wagon off to one side holds the day's supply of manure, ready to be carried outside the walls for use on the fields."],"exits":[{"to":165,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":168,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":207,"exit":"go","move":"go stable"}]},
  {"id":168,"x":-80,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Eastgate Road","descriptions":["A tanner's shop emits a pungent odor of ammonia and other, less palatable odors.  Flayed hides, scraped clean of hair, are lashed to wooden stretchers and set to dry.  The tanner's apprentices work around open vats in the courtyard beside the building, soaking fresh skins in noxious solutions of ammonia and salts or dying tanned leather to order for a customer."],"exits":[{"to":167,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":169,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":209,"exit":"go","move":"go shop"}]},
  {"id":169,"x":-80,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Eastgate Road","descriptions":["Ten tall wooden towers hold the town's supply of grain against the winter months, with space enough to walk around below.  Barley, wheat, oats, rye and corn - all are stored against the coming cold.  Tiny hovels built from peeled logs and patchy plaster chinking huddle beneath the silos, homes for the town's poorer residents."],"exits":[{"to":168,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":170,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":208,"exit":"go","move":"go shop"}]},
  {"id":170,"x":-80,"y":190,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Eastgate Road","descriptions":["A wooden watch tower, little more than an open shack on tall stilts, overlooks the town walls.  The stone curtain wall does not yet extend this far to the south around the town, but the tower provides a shelter of sorts for guards patrolling the palisade's upper walkway."],"exits":[{"to":169,"exit":"north","move":"north"}]},
  {"id":171,"x":-80,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Eastgate Road","descriptions":["Log houses chinked with pale plaster line the narrow, winding street.  Workmen have been demolishing poorly built shacks huddled along the inner palisade to make way for the new stone curtain wall under construction.  Wagons bringing in building stone and carrying away lumber for use elsewhere leave deep ruts in the dirt road.  Towering above the small houses, a fortress rises on a steep hill to the west, overlooking the rest of the town."],"exits":[{"to":172,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":165,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":172,"x":-80,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Eastgate Road","descriptions":["A patch of marigolds struggle for survival in a small garden beside the road, beaten down by the heavy boots of the workers constructing the curtain wall.  The houses are built close together, most sharing a common wall with its neighbors on either side.  Fire must remain an ever-present danger in the tiny village."],"exits":[{"to":173,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":171,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":173,"x":-80,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Eastgate Road","descriptions":["A stone drum tower rises at the corner of the wooden palisades.  Completed prior to the building of the stone walls, the tower offers a vantage point for guards keeping watch over the fields around the town, as well as housing for those not currently on duty.  The smell of baking bread wafts through the air from some nearby inn or housewife's kitchen."],"exits":[{"to":172,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":174,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":174,"x":-100,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Northwall Road","descriptions":["Built against the wooden palisade, the town's sole tavern does a brisk business day and night.  Uniformed guardsmen, shopkeepers, fishermen and herdsmen wander in and out for a pint of ale or a bite to eat."],"exits":[{"to":173,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":175,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":206,"exit":"go","move":"go tavern"}]},
  {"id":175,"x":-120,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Northwall Road","descriptions":["Thatched roofed cottages huddle together in the shadows of the log palisade surrounding the town.  Carvings decorate the exposed timber beams -- on one house, a gargoyle hunched beneath the eaves, on another, dark brown roses peep out amidst the pale white plaster.  Flimsy stalls against the outer wall can be quickly set up and dismantled on market days."],"exits":[{"to":174,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":176,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":176,"x":-140,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Northwall Road","descriptions":["Cattle mill about in an enclosed common area, shifting drowsily in the darkness.  The sweet scent of roses drifts on the night air, not quite masking the smell of the animals.  Torches flicker high above on the hill as the guards make their rounds of the keep walls.","Workers muck out a muddy field, shoveling the dung left by the village's cattle into a small wicker-sided cart.  Sweet scented roses grow in profusion around the common area, enclosing it with their thorns and ameliorating the smell."],"exits":[{"to":175,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":178,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":177,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":177,"x":-160,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Northwall Road","descriptions":["The road narrows to be simply a packed dirt path that runs along the eastern end of the soldiers' drill field to a small gate in the walls.  Too narrow for a wagon or cart, the gate allows drovers to herd the town's cattle out to graze during the day."],"exits":[{"to":176,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":211,"exit":"go","move":"go gate"}]},
  {"id":178,"x":-140,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Waterway Road","descriptions":["Lazy tendrils of smoke curl up from the chimneys on either end of a long thatched-roof barracks, quickly dissipating into nothingness.  Situated behind the main building, smaller brick structures huddle along the edge of the keep's outermost ditch to the west."],"exits":[{"to":176,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":179,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":203,"exit":"go","move":"go barracks"}]},
  {"id":179,"x":-140,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Waterway Road","descriptions":["A small store does a brisk business as shoppers stride in and out with baskets over their arms.  The sign over the entry is painted with the image of a juggler tossing a ham, a dagger and a skull.  To the west, a cobbled road begins its climb up a steep incline toward the keep that towers over the rest of the town."],"exits":[{"to":178,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":180,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":186,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":202,"exit":"go","move":"go store"}]},
  {"id":180,"x":-140,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Waterway Road","descriptions":["Most houses in the town are built side-by-side, sharing their walls with their neighbors.  Here, however, a narrow cobblestone alley has been left between two buildings, flanked by a woven wicker gate.  Scraggly rose bushes growing on either side twine their thorny branches to form a fragrant arch over the passage."],"exits":[{"to":179,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":181,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":187,"exit":"go","move":"go gate"}]},
  {"id":181,"x":-140,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Waterway Road","descriptions":["Sheaves of grain and flowers bound with dark green vines decorate the doors of a small church.  Unlike the other buildings in town, the church has been finished with split-wood shingles and stone walls.  A small garden surrounds the walls, filled with fruit trees, dawns-eye daisies and morning glories."],"exits":[{"to":180,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":182,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":200,"exit":"go","move":"go church"}]},
  {"id":182,"x":-160,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Waterway Road","descriptions":["Dark brown cowhides are visible beneath the thatched roofs on nearby buildings.  Soaked with water, the skins reduce the risk of fire in close-packed wooden structures.  Several of the houses have mirrored glass witch balls, traditionally believed to ward off evil, hanging from the windows."],"exits":[{"to":181,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":183,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":183,"x":-180,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Waterway Road","descriptions":["Waves of heat and the smell of fresh bread billow out the open door of a nearby brick bakery.  Few houses have the luxury of their own oven, so local housewives bring their daily meals to the baker to cook in his."],"exits":[{"to":182,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":184,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":199,"exit":"go","move":"go bakery"}]},
  {"id":184,"x":-200,"y":190,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Waterway Road","descriptions":["Visitors to the town can find shelter for the night at a nearby guesthouse.  A sign, painted with a picture of a hart resting its head in a woman's lap, sways over the porch railing.  Neatly tended window boxes are home to a colorful jumble of flowers, and the door is open to all."],"exits":[{"to":183,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":185,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":197,"exit":"go","move":"go guesthouse"},{"to":197,"exit":"go","move":"go guest"}]},
  {"id":185,"x":-220,"y":210,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Waterway Road","descriptions":["A door in the town walls reveals a rope ladder dangling over the edge of the cliff, leading down to the river bank far below.  In times of attack, the ladder can be drawn up to repel invaders, or the rope may simply be cut, ensuring the town's security.  Two mules hitched to a windlass drive a counter-weighted wooden platform used to haul packages up from the docks."],"exits":[{"to":184,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":191,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"},{"to":298,"exit":"go","move":"go building"}]},
  {"id":186,"x":-200,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Foregate Bridge","descriptions":["A steep-sided ditch runs the length of the village, separating the town from Rossgallan Keep.  The western side of the earthwork is higher than the eastern and topped by a spiked wooden palisade wall.  Anyone wishing to enter the keep must cross a narrow drawbridge, no wider than a single cart, flanked by wooden guard towers on either end."],"exits":[{"to":179,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":201,"exit":"go","move":"go drawbridge"}],"aliases":["Foregate Bridge","bridge"]},
  {"id":187,"x":-120,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Narrow Alley","descriptions":["Nestled in the shadow of a small church to the south, a tiny thatched-roof cottage squats at the end of the alley.  Beyond it, a grassy courtyard between the rows of houses provides a gathering place for residents of the town."],"exits":[{"to":188,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":180,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":272,"exit":"go","move":"go cottage"}],"aliases":["Narrow Alley"]},
  {"id":188,"x":-100,"y":110,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Grassy Courtyard","descriptions":["The town's houses present a severe face to the city streets, but their back doors lead to a riot of color in this grassy courtyard.  Running the length of the town, the wide strip provides a safe place for children to play and small gardens for each resident.  Dovecotes and chicken coops huddle behind each house, extending the village food supplies."],"exits":[{"to":189,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":190,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":187,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":189,"x":-100,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Grassy Courtyard","descriptions":["Fragrant herbs grow in cheerful clusters at the northern end of the courtyard.  Rosemary and lavender, chives and rue, colorful blue-flowered wolfsbane and lemon balm all perfume the air with a heady fragrance.  In one corner, an angled turf bench covered with creeping thyme releases its scent every time a visitor sits down to enjoy the surroundings."],"exits":[{"to":188,"exit":"south","move":"south"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":190,"x":-100,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Grassy Courtyard","descriptions":["Wild rose bushes bloom in sweet profusion, their thorny stems clinging to a whitewashed pergola.  Wooden benches nestled beneath the lattice structure provide a place for housewives to gossip during the day, sheltered from the sun, or lovers to meet at night."],"exits":[{"to":188,"exit":"north","move":"north"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":191,"x":-220,"y":230,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, River's Edge","descriptions":["Workers bustle about, carrying boxes and crates between the docks, a warehouse and a counter-weighted wooden platform.  The Traders' Guild crest is prominently displayed over the lintel of a sturdy brick building off to one side.  Burly guards keep a watchful eye on their surroundings, always prepared to sound the alarm in case of intruders."],"exits":[{"to":192,"exit":"go","move":"go dock"},{"to":185,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"},{"to":193,"exit":"go","move":"go build"}]},
  {"id":192,"x":-220,"y":250,"z":0,"title":"Lake Gwenalion, Rossman's Landing Dock","descriptions":["The green waters of Lake Gwenalion darken with silt from the Jantspyre River as the two merge here at Rossman's Landing.  Fishing boats and private craft keep the dock workers busy repairing nets, salting and drying the day's catch or shifting cargo between ship and town."],"exits":[{"to":191,"exit":"go","move":"go shore"}],"color":"#FF00FF","aliases":["Dock"]},
  {"id":193,"x":-210,"y":230,"z":0,"title":"Traders' Guild Outpost, Foyer","descriptions":["Metal bars cover the tall, narrow windows, allowing little light to filter through.  Candles chase away the shadows of the foyer, bringing warmth to the cold hall."],"exits":[{"to":191,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":194,"exit":"go","move":"go shop"},{"to":195,"exit":"go","move":"go vault"}],"aliases":["Trader Outpost"]},
  {"id":194,"x":-210,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Traders' Guild Outpost, Gem Shop","descriptions":["Thick tapers hang in a wrought iron chandelier, shedding their light over the plush grey carpet and pale walls.  An assortment of tools lie on a velvet-topped lapidary's bench, padded to prevent damage to the precious gems.  Working with scales and loupe, the goldsmith examines each stone for flaws and determines its value before bagging it and storing it away in a strongbox."],"exits":[{"to":193,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Gems"]},
  {"id":195,"x":-200,"y":230,"z":0,"title":"Traders' Guild Outpost, Depository","descriptions":["Footsteps are muffled by the plush brown carpet and paneled walls of the depository.  No mere ostentation, the soft, dark surfaces allow clerks to easily spot any spilled coins, and keep them from rolling away.  Young traders work under the careful supervision of their masters, always alert for any possible pilfering."],"exits":[{"to":193,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":196,"exit":"go","move":"go booth"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Teller"]},
  {"id":196,"x":-200,"y":240,"z":0,"title":"Traders' Guild Outpost, Exchange","descriptions":["Neatly labeled coffers hold coins of various demonimations and currencies, all arranged on shelves lining the paneled walls.  As in the outer room, plush brown carpet cushions the floor, preventing any dropped coin from rolling away.  Apprentices labor beneath the watchful eyes of Master Traders, counting coins and making change for visitors to the booth."],"exits":[{"to":195,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Exchange"]},
  {"id":197,"x":-210,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Hartsease Guesthouse, Entry","descriptions":["Armchairs and couches in muted shades of plum and ecru surround a cheerfully glowing fire in the entry hall.  Vases of fresh flowers on the side tables fill the room with a spicy fragrance that mingles with the sharp tang of apple wood smoke.  Run by Hartsease Weaver, a widow, the building features dormitory style accommodations and a common room where guests may eat the food they bring with them."],"exits":[{"to":184,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":198,"exit":"go","move":"go room"}],"aliases":["Hartsease Guesthouse"]},
  {"id":198,"x":-220,"y":180,"z":0,"title":"Hartsease Guesthouse, Common Room","descriptions":["Sturdy rectory tables and low benches offer a quiet place to eat and drink food brought with you or bought from the nearby bakery.  At the back of the room, the door leading to the kitchen and the owner's private quarters is half-hidden by a rice paper screen."],"exits":[{"to":197,"exit":"out","move":"out"}]},
  {"id":199,"x":-190,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Goldbricker's Bakery","descriptions":["Heat pours off the brick ovens along the far wall.  The baker and his apprentices bustle about, kneading bread, chopping wood and performing other mundane tasks.  Near the door, a wood-slatted baker's rack displays the day's wares."],"exits":[{"to":183,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Goldbricker's Bakery","Bakery"]},
  {"id":200,"x":-150,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Church","descriptions":["A stained glass window fills the eastern wall, situated to catch the rising sun.  Beneath it, the altar is covered by a grass-green velvet cloth embroidered with images of cows and grain to honor the goddess Berengaria.  Sheaves of wheat bound with ribbons decorate the walls of this simple village church."],"exits":[{"to":181,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#A6A3D9","aliases":["Shrine2-06","Berengaria","Church","Depart"]},
  {"id":201,"x":-260,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Foregate","descriptions":["From the top of the motte, the lights of the town spread out to the east, about twenty feet below.  A steep wooden drawbridge leads down, over the ditches at the base of the hill, to the streets of Rossman's Landing.  Rossgallan Keep is guarded by a palisade fence -- sharpened wooden posts sunk deep in the ground around the flat hilltop -- which is broken only by a heavy iron-banded gate.","From the top of the motte, the thatched roofs of the town spread out to the east, about twenty feet below.  A steep wooden drawbridge leads down, over the ditches at the base of the hill, to the streets of Rossman's Landing.  Rossgallan Keep is guarded by a palisade fence -- sharpened wooden posts sunk deep in the ground around the flat hilltop -- which is broken only by a heavy iron-banded gate."],"exits":[{"to":186,"exit":"go","move":"go drawbridge"},{"to":227,"exit":"go","move":"go gate"}]},
  {"id":202,"x":-130,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Jester's General Store, Salesroom","descriptions":["The salesroom is packed almost to the bursting point -- boxes filled with weapons piled next to barrels of bows and baskets of small beanbags.  A narrow path winds its way in a serpentine fashion past bolts of cloth and a rack of clothes.  Even the rafters are laden with hams, cheeses and other foodstuffs.  Eauin Jester, the store's owner, does a brisk business."],"exits":[{"to":179,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Jester's General Store","General"]},
  {"id":203,"x":-130,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Guard Barracks, Mess Hall","descriptions":["Wooden benches surround simple planed-board tables in the mess hall.  Used for meals, the room is also a popular gathering place for off-duty guardsmen seeking a game of cards, dice or chess, or a comfortable place to sit while honing a sword or patching a leather jerkin."],"exits":[{"to":178,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":204,"exit":"go","move":"go door"},{"to":205,"exit":"go","move":"go kitchen"}],"aliases":["Barracks"]},
  {"id":204,"x":-120,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Guard Barracks, Dormitory","descriptions":["Rows of bunks stacked one atop the other line the walls of the room.  A wooden trunk at the bottom and between each set of bunks holds a guard's personal belongings.  Swinging doors separate the dormitory from the mess hall."],"exits":[{"to":203,"exit":"go","move":"go door"}]},
  {"id":205,"x":-120,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Guard Barracks, Kitchen","descriptions":["Brick ovens line the back wall, heating the building in the winter.  Piles of potatoes, beans and rice are held in wicker bins near the door.  On the stove, soup simmers gently, and a basket of fruit offers between-meal snacks for the town's guards."],"exits":[{"to":203,"exit":"out","move":"out"}]},
  {"id":206,"x":-100,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Portman's Tavern, Common Room","descriptions":["Little more than the front room of Portman's house, the tavern features benches framing the brick fireplace and four tables with just enough room to squeeze into the chairs.  A barmaid offers stew and ale as she makes her rounds of the patrons, collecting her coins before a drop is served."],"exits":[{"to":174,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Portman's Tavern","Tavern"]},
  {"id":207,"x":-90,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Skipstone Stables","descriptions":["Sturdy wooden stalls line the walls of the stable, each with their own manger and water bucket.  A thick layer of clean straw bedding covers the floor, cushioning the animals' feet, and tack is neatly slung over the wall between the stalls.  Behind the building, a small corral gives the beasts room to exercise."],"exits":[{"to":167,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Skipstone Stables","Stable"]},
  {"id":208,"x":-90,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"A. R. Cayne's Majikul Serplize","descriptions":["Dilapidated piles of clutter lean at odd angles in the tiny shop, leaving little room for shoppers to browse amidst the peculiar assortments of wares.  An old birdcage hangs from the rafters above a slate-topped worktable, while buckets and coffers vie for space with a porcelain hair cache and a large iron cauldron."],"exits":[{"to":169,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":210,"exit":"go","move":"go door"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["A. R. Cayne's Majikul Serplize","Magic"]},
  {"id":209,"x":-90,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Drinak's Tannery","descriptions":["Sweet rushes strewn with strongly scented herbs cushion the floor but do little to eliminate the rank stench of the vats in the courtyard outside.  Piles of furs bound into bales sit around the room, waiting to be shipped."],"exits":[{"to":168,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Drinak's Tannery","Bundles"]},
  {"id":210,"x":-100,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"A. R. Cayne's Majikul Serplize, Broom Closet","descriptions":["As always, the dirtiest room seems to be the one in which the brooms are kept hanging in clusters from wooden pegs.  Mounds of dust are carelessly swept under the scrap of rug on the floor, and mouse droppings litter the corners with careless abandon.  A wooden door leads back to the main sales floor."],"exits":[{"to":208,"exit":"go","move":"go door"}],"color":"#FF0000"},
  {"id":211,"x":-160,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, At the Gate","descriptions":["A weathered wooden gate is set securely into a tall palisade wall stretching two stories high.  The fresh breeze fights a losing battle in its effort to mask the smell of the cattle that pass through daily to graze on the fragrant grass.","A weathered wooden gate is suspended between a section of palisade wall that rises two stories high.  The rich, fragrant grass of the meadow competes in vain with the smell of the animals brought here to graze."],"exits":[{"to":212,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":223,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":222,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":177,"exit":"go","move":"go gate"}],"aliases":["Shepherd's Meadow"]},
  {"id":212,"x":-160,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["Torch light flickers in the windows of the keep that overlooks the town to the southwest.  Patches of sweet clover grow at the edge of the split rail fence that runs along the western border of this meadow.","The silk standard atop the keep in the distance snaps in a sudden breeze.  Undulating grass underfoot provides rich feed for the cattle that graze nearby."],"exits":[{"to":213,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":226,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":223,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":222,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":211,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":213,"x":-160,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["Starlight glints off the surface of an empty bottle lying forgotten in the grass beneath the split rail fence.  To the east, the meadow spreads out in golden glory.","An empty bottle lies beneath the split rail fence, lodged under matted grass, perhaps left by a local farmer who paused to refresh himself.  Insects buzz incessantly around a small pile of manure, their discordant hum a basso counterpoint to the high bleating of sheep, grazing in the distance."],"exits":[{"to":214,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":215,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":226,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":223,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":212,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":214,"x":-160,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["Soft starlight kisses the tops of trees in the near distance to the north, marking the edge of a large wood.  The meadow stretches southward, a golden blanket of rich feed for the cattle that graze here.","Marking out the northernmost boundary of the grazing pasture, the split rail fence turns sharply off to the east here.  In the distance to the north, the beginning of a large wood evinces itself, populated with trees stretching their branches in supplication toward the sky."],"exits":[{"to":215,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":226,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":213,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":215,"x":-140,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["The canopy of the heavens gazes peacefully over this wide field of grass.  The weathered split rail fence along the northern border is draped in shadow, and the scurrying of tiny woodland creatures can be heard, breaking the silence of the night.","The wind-weathered uprights of the split rail fence march stolidly into the distance, marking out the northern boundary of this verdant pasture.  The sweet trill of a bluebird calling to his mate sparkles on the fresh breeze."],"exits":[{"to":216,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":225,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":226,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":213,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":214,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":216,"x":-120,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["Diamond-bright dewdrops cling to the petals of a group of jes-roses that has somehow escaped the notice of the animals feasting on the tender grass of the meadow.","A solitary clump of fragrant jes-roses takes refuge here against the split rail fence, a sweet delicacy somehow missed by the grazing animals in the meadow."],"exits":[{"to":217,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":218,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":225,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":226,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":215,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":217,"x":-100,"y":-50,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["Carefully stacked building implements and lengths of unfinished wood cast long shadows here in the northeast corner of the meadow.  The faint odor of cooked meat and wood smoke lingers in the night air, betraying the recent presence of fence menders who used this as a gathering place to eat and rest.","Various building implements and lengths of unfinished wood are stacked here in the northeast corner of the meadow, awaiting future repairs to the split rail fence.  A stone fire ring and the scattered bones of small animals indicate this clearing might have been used as a gathering place for builders to eat and have a brief rest from their labors."],"exits":[{"to":218,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":225,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":216,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#C2B280","aliases":["RTT22","RT-SM-MF"]},
  {"id":218,"x":-100,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["A large rock, expertly detoured by the split rail fence, casts a proprietary shadow over the rich grass of this field.  The evening air gently brushes the heads of the gathering of wildflowers at its base.","The split rail fence detours around a large rock the builders must not have been able to move.  Wildflowers grow in profusion around its base, as if staking out their own territory."],"exits":[{"to":217,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":219,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":224,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":225,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":216,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":219,"x":-100,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["Gentle starlight shines through the leaves of a towering oak tree that stands benevolently on the other side of the split rail fence.  From the close-cropped grass beneath, the scurrying of small nocturnal creatures can be heard.","Occasionally a bright-eyed squirrel stops to perch atop the split rail fence, seeking acorns from the mighty oak tree that towers majestically overhead.  The rippling grasses of the meadow offer up the scent of wildflowers along with the droppings of cattle."],"exits":[{"to":218,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":220,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":221,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":224,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":225,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":220,"x":-100,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["Pale celestial light crowns the top of a stone drum tower situated here at the corner of the palisade wall.  Sentries pass back and forth across its eastern edge, alert for the presence of invaders.","The looming shadow of a stone drum tower falls across this corner of the meadow.  Sentries pace its outer edge, casting a watchful eye over the eastern border of the palisade."],"exits":[{"to":219,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":221,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":224,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":221,"x":-120,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["Muffled sounds of song and laughter float across the palisade wall on the night air.  The gentle breeze ruffles the sweet grass of this verdant meadow, like a whisper of forgotten music.","Snatches of song and merriment drift across the palisade wall, borne on the gentle breeze.  From time to time, a startled field mouse scurries through the grass, perhaps seeking escape from a predator on the wing."],"exits":[{"to":224,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":219,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":220,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":222,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":223,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":222,"x":-140,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["The night sky gazes peacefully over this wide field of aromatic grass that stretches northward into the distance.  To the southwest, a keep stands on a hill, a sentinel against invaders.","Sweet smelling grass, about waist-high on a Halfling, shows signs of recent voracious grazing by a large number of herd animals, perhaps cattle or sheep.  In the distance to the southwest, a keep rises over the land, ever watchful against invaders."],"exits":[{"to":223,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":224,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":221,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":211,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":212,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":223,"x":-140,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["The scattered wildflowers in the grass of the verdant meadow have closed for the night.  An occasional owl swoops low, and with a flash of talons, captures its evening meal.","Wildflowers are scattered among the waving grass of the wide field, dotting the landscape with bright spots of color.  Occasionally the bleating of sheep can be heard, carried on the breeze."],"exits":[{"to":226,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":225,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":224,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":221,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":222,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":211,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":212,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":213,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":224,"x":-120,"y":-10,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["A sentry gives a staccato cry atop the stone tower to the southwest, breaking the stillness of the evening air.  The fresh herbal scent of the grass underfoot mingles with the smell of animals.","Sturdy stonework and vigilant sentries top a drum tower to the southeast, testimony to attacks against the gentle folk of Rossman's Landing.  The ground underfoot is packed by the passage of hooves, the meadow grass cropped short by grazing animals."],"exits":[{"to":225,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":218,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":219,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":220,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":221,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":222,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":223,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":226,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":225,"x":-120,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["The evening breeze lifts the leaves of the old hickory tree that stands here, carrying the scent of wildflowers and wood smoke.","A stalwart hickory tree rises from the rippling grass, its thick branches offering an expanse of sweet shade around moss-covered roots."],"exits":[{"to":216,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":217,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":218,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":219,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":224,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":223,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":226,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":215,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":226,"x":-140,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Shepherd's Meadow, Grazing Land","descriptions":["Starlight pools in the hollows formed by the scattered clumps of grass.  A soft rustling heralds the approach of a brown rabbit, heading home to his burrow.","A tawny brown rabbit pops in and out of view among the hummocks of sweet grass, heading home to his burrow nearby.  The sprightly breeze carries an herbal scent mixed with the smell of animals."],"exits":[{"to":215,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":216,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":225,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":224,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":223,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":212,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":213,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":214,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":227,"x":-280,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Eastcourt Gate","descriptions":["Built on a flat-topped hill above the rest of the town, the keep consists of a grassy torch-lit courtyard surrounded by a wooden palisade fence.  Small buildings dot the perimeter of the enclosure, the furthest ones visible only as lighted windows in the darkness.  A long two-story manor occupies the western side of the courtyard, housing the Rossman family and their personal retainers, and watch fires burn atop the octagonal towers along the north and south walls.","Built on a flat-topped hill above the rest of the town, the keep consists of a grassy courtyard surrounded by a wooden palisade fence.  Small buildings dot the perimeter of the enclosure, with orchards and grazing areas in the center.  A long two-story manor occupies the western side of the courtyard, housing the Rossman family and their personal retainers, and octagonal towers provide lookout posts along the north and south walls."],"exits":[{"to":238,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":228,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":246,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":240,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":243,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":201,"exit":"go","move":"go gate"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":228,"x":-280,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Southeast Courtyard","descriptions":["Smoke and soot drift from the southeast, darkening the timber and plaster walls of a small shop and the wooden posts of the palisade beyond.  A sign swaying above the shop's door bears the painted image of a fist clutching a sword."],"exits":[{"to":227,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":229,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":246,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":240,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":270,"exit":"go","move":"go shop"}]},
  {"id":229,"x":-310,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Southeast Courtyard","descriptions":["Though quieter than during the daytime, the ring of hammers against metal still resounds as blacksmiths ply their trade in a nearby forge.  One of the only stone buildings within the keep, sparks billow forth in the darkness as someone within pumps the bellows, sending a wave of heat eastward across the courtyard.","The ring of hammers against metal resounds as blacksmiths ply their trade in a nearby forge.  One of the only stone buildings within the keep, sparks and soot billow forth from the chimney stack as someone within pumps the bellows, sending a cloud of smoke drifting eastward across the courtyard."],"exits":[{"to":246,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":228,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":230,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":247,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":230,"x":-340,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Southcourt Tower","descriptions":["At the southern end of the keep, a high wooden tower, twin to one to the north, rises above the palisade wall, offering a commanding view of the areas surrounding the town."],"exits":[{"to":247,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":246,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":229,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":231,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":239,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":295,"exit":"go","move":"go tower"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":231,"x":-370,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Southwest Courtyard","descriptions":["South of the jousting field, a stable is home to the keep's horses.  Massive animals, able to charge even while bearing the weight of full barding plus that of a man in armor, shift restlessly in the darkness of their fenced-in pasture.","South of the jousting field, a stable is home to the keep's horses.  Massive animals, able to charge even while bearing the weight of full barding plus that of a man in armor, nicker softly in the fenced-in pasture."],"exits":[{"to":239,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":247,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":230,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":232,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":250,"exit":"go","move":"go stable"}]},
  {"id":232,"x":-400,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Southwest Courtyard","descriptions":["The ripe fragrance of the horses grazing in a pen behind the stable to the southeast permeates the area, identifying the building even in the darkness.  A small kennel attached to the building houses drowsy hunting dogs.  Other animals shift from foot to foot as they sleep, clustered about each other within a makeshift rope enclosure.","The ripe fragrance of the horses grazing in a pen behind the stable to the southeast permeates the area, drawing flies that are as attracted to the nearby manure pile as to horses themselves.  Hunting dogs bay within a kennel attached to the building.  Other animals freely roam the courtyard, cropping the grass and swishing their tails irritably at the children charged with chasing them away from the Keep's gardens."],"exits":[{"to":233,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":242,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":239,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":231,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":249,"exit":"go","move":"go kennel"}]},
  {"id":233,"x":-400,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, West Courtyard","descriptions":["Wooden torches flicker in the darkness, sending shadows stretching up the palisade wall and emphasizing the dark places between the bundles of thatch mounded atop the roof of a nearby chapel.  Two wooden ravens face each other above the lintel of the door, one on either side of a saturnine carved face.  Careful craftsmanship and attention to the least significant detail makes this not only a shelter for worshippers, but an offering of the craftsman's labor to the greater glory of Kertigen.","In the shadow of the western wall, bundles of golden thatch mound atop the roof of a nearby chapel.  Two wooden ravens face each other above the lintel of the door, one on either side of a benevolent carved face.  Careful craftsmanship and attention to the least significant detail makes this not only a shelter for worshippers, but an offering of the craftsman's labor to the greater glory of Kertigen."],"exits":[{"to":234,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":245,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":242,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":239,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":232,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":248,"exit":"go","move":"go chapel"}]},
  {"id":234,"x":-400,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Northwest Courtyard","descriptions":["A large manor house nestles in the northwest corner of the courtyard.  Little is visible in the darkness but the pale plaster walls and the flickering glow of torches or candles behind closed shutters.  The faint scent of smoke drifts up from the chimney of a small stone kitchen beside the manor.","A large manor house nestles in the northwest corner of the courtyard.  Two stories tall, with exposed beams and white lime plaster, the house is topped by a clay tile roof broken by several shuttered dormers.  Beside it, smoke drifts up from the chimney of a low stone kitchen."],"exits":[{"to":235,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":245,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":242,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":233,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":253,"exit":"go","move":"go house"},{"to":260,"exit":"go","move":"go kitchen","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":235,"x":-370,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Northwest Courtyard","descriptions":["A pair of targets, one red, one brown, are mounted on split logs in this corner of the courtyard.  Hard to make out in the flickering torchlight, a few gouges in the palisade mark the places where the archers have missed, imbedding their arrows in the wooden wall around the keep.","A pair of targets, one red, one brown, are mounted on split logs in this corner of the courtyard.  Scuff marks in the grass show where the targets have been moved closer or further away from the firing line, and a few gouges in the palisade mark the places where the archers have missed, imbedding their arrows in the wooden wall around the keep."],"exits":[{"to":236,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":244,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":245,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":234,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":265,"exit":"go","move":"go hut"}]},
  {"id":236,"x":-340,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Northcourt Tower","descriptions":["Watch fires flare atop the two wooden towers rising up over the palisade fence that surrounds the motte, one here in the center of the north wall and a matching tower in the center of the south.  The tower provides shelter for guards on duty and access to the covered walkway along the top of the walls.","Two wooden towers rise up over the palisade fence that surrounds the motte, one here in the center of the north wall and a matching tower in the center of the south.  The tower provides shelter for guards on duty and access to the covered walkway along the top of the walls."],"exits":[{"to":237,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":243,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":244,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":245,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":235,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":273,"exit":"go","move":"go tower"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":237,"x":-310,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Northeast Courtyard","descriptions":["Grass grows in a smoothly cropped lawn beneath the gnarled branches of fruit trees.  The tree trunks block the light from the torches around the perimeter of the keep, enveloping you in darkness.","Green grass grows in a smoothly cropped lawn beneath the gnarled branches of fruit trees.  The high walls of the palisade shelter the trees from the cold winter winds, without blocking the sunlight needed for growth."],"exits":[{"to":238,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":243,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":244,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":236,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"color":"#00FFFF","aliases":["Fruit Trees"]},
  {"id":238,"x":-280,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Northeast Courtyard","descriptions":["Wisps of fragrant smoke drift through the air, most strongly near a stone smokehouse.  Several small buildings huddle in the darkness around the bases of tall wooden silos.","Wisps of fragrant smoke drift out of a stone smokehouse where hams and fish are hung to preserve them for the cold season.  Several small buildings cluster around the bases of tall wooden silos filled with grain."],"exits":[{"to":227,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":240,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":243,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":237,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":269,"exit":"go","move":"go smokehouse"}],"color":"#00FFFF"},
  {"id":239,"x":-370,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Courtyard","descriptions":["Splintered wooden pells lie discarded in a pile to one side of a practice field.  To the south, a rail fence encloses the jousting grounds, now quiet in the darkness.","Splintered wooden pells lie discarded in a pile to one side of a practice field.  To the south, a rail fence encloses the jousting grounds where the keep's fighters practice riding and tilting against wooden barrels and other obstacles or against each other."],"exits":[{"to":242,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":241,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":247,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":230,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":231,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":232,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":233,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":240,"x":-310,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Courtyard","descriptions":["A long, low building nestles beneath a high thatched roof at the eastern end of the courtyard, giving it an odd resemblance to an elongated haystack with a chimney at either end.  The steep angle of the roof helps keep snow from accumulating during the winters."],"exits":[{"to":243,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":238,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":227,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":228,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":246,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":247,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":241,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":244,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":241,"x":-340,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Courtyard","descriptions":["Pale gravel paths contrast vividly with the cropped green grass that covers the enclosed motte.  Small buildings dot the perimeter of the grounds, while twin towers, one to the north, one to the south, loom in the distance above the palisade walls."],"exits":[{"to":244,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":243,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":240,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":246,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":247,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":239,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":242,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":245,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}],"aliases":["Rossgallan Keep"]},
  {"id":242,"x":-370,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Courtyard","descriptions":["Low stone benches, pale in night's deep shadows, cluster in a circle beneath the spreading branches of a mistwood tree.  The scents of sweet pea blossoms and roses drift through the evening air, perfuming the darkness with their fragrance.  An occasional nicker of a restless horse drifts through the darkness from the south.","Low stone benches cluster in a circle beneath the shade of a spreading mistwood tree.  Sweet pea blossoms, roses and other fragrant flowers perfume the air, making this gentle bower a delightful place to sit and sew for the ladies of the keep as they watch the exertions of the warriors in the practice fields to the south."],"exits":[{"to":245,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":244,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":241,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":247,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":239,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":232,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":233,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":234,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":243,"x":-310,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Courtyard","descriptions":["Low-cropped grass stretches out across the courtyard, broken by gravel paths leading from building to building.  To the west, candlelight lends a golden glow to the windows of a two-story manor, its pale plastered walls barely visible in the darkness.","Low-cropped grass stretches out across the courtyard, broken by gravel paths leading from building to building.  To the west, a two-story manor dominates the others in the keep, with a clay tile roof instead of thatch, and plastered and half-timbered walls instead of whitewashed wood."],"exits":[{"to":237,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":238,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":227,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":240,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":241,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":244,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":236,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":244,"x":-340,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Courtyard","descriptions":["Spilled water and foot traffic churn the ground beside the keep's well to mud, only somewhat controlled by the gravel on the path around it.  A small ring of moss-covered rocks surrounds the well itself, with a slanted split-shingled roof to keep the leaves out of the water.  Nearby wooden benches offer a place for courting couples to enjoy stolen moments in the darkness before returning with the water to kitchen, barracks or anywhere else it may be needed.","Spilled water and foot traffic churn the ground beside the keep's well to mud, only somewhat controlled by the gravel on the path around it.  A small ring of moss-covered rocks surrounds the well itself, with a slanted split-shingled roof to keep the leaves out of the water.  Nearby wooden benches offer a place to rest a bucket or to sit for a companionable gossip before carrying the bucket to kitchen, barracks or anywhere else it may be needed."],"exits":[{"to":236,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":237,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":243,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":240,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":241,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":242,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":245,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":235,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":245,"x":-370,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Courtyard","descriptions":["The sharp tang of medicinal and kitchen herbs perfume the gardens, unseen in the darkness.  Pale white muslin cloches cluster in long rows, sheltering berries or other tender plants from the cool night air.  The shoulder-high wicker frameworks behind a low bench provide a decorative accent, as well as support for peas and beans during the growing season.","Medicinal and kitchen herbs grow in neatly kept rows, perfuming the air with their sharp fragrance.  Other beds hold root vegetables, thickly mulched with salt hay, or tender leafy greens and berries growing beneath the shelter of a muslin cloche.  The shoulder-high wicker frameworks behind a low bench provide a decorative accent, as well as support for peas and beans during the growing season."],"exits":[{"to":235,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":236,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":244,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":241,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":242,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":233,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":234,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":246,"x":-310,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Courtyard","descriptions":["Vats of foul-smelling liquid squat in the grassy yard of a nearby cottage, knee-high obstacles in the darkness.  A low structure along the side houses a few chickens drowsily huddled in their roosts.","Vats of dye splattered in rainbow hues stand in the grassy yard of a nearby cottage, while hanks of yarn and drapes of fabric hang from rattan racks to dry.  From time to time, chickens nose about, scratching at the grass in their ongoing hunt for fallen grains."],"exits":[{"to":240,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":227,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":228,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":229,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":230,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":247,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":241,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":271,"exit":"go","move":"go cottage"}]},
  {"id":247,"x":-340,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Courtyard","descriptions":["Wood shavings litter the ground beside a small workshop, left over from the day's work.  Barrel staves, stacked in neat piles beside the building, await the attentions of the cooper.  A small sign, carved with a picture of a mallet and wood chisel, sways above the workshop's open door, and candles within the shop cast a golden glow over finely wrought cabinetry on display.","Wood shavings litter the ground beside a small workshop as apprentices labor with chamfers to form the staves for barrels, the end results stacked in neat piles beside the building awaiting the attentions of the cooper.  A small sign, carved with a picture of a mallet and wood chisel, sways above the workshop's open door, through which is visible finely wrought cabinetry made by the master craftsman."],"exits":[{"to":241,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":240,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":246,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":229,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":230,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":231,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":239,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":242,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":266,"exit":"go","move":"go workshop"}]},
  {"id":248,"x":-410,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Chapel of Kertigen","descriptions":["Polished mistwood, carved with vertical panels of ravens, raccoons, and welkins, adorns the walls of the chapel.  No pews offer places to sit, but the bare stone floor is softened by a few prayer rugs for worshippers.  At the front of the chapel, a wide carved panel depicts a bearded man with a raven perched upon his shoulder, with smaller side panels showing a woodcarver helped by a welkin, and a saturnine man watching a raccoon play with a broken cartwheel."],"exits":[{"to":233,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["Chapel of Kertigen","Kertigen's chapel"]},
  {"id":249,"x":-410,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Kennel","descriptions":["An assortment of dogs, confined in simple willow pens, bay noisily as the assistant kennel-master moves about tending to their needs.  The kennel contains no lady's lap dogs, just working dogs that guard the local sheep or work the boats on the lake, or hunting dogs bred to pursue everything from rabbits to deer."],"exits":[{"to":232,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Kennel"]},
  {"id":250,"x":-380,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Stables","descriptions":["Half-height wooden walls divide the stable into individual stalls, with a wide aisle running the length of the building.  Layers of straw on the floor cushion the hoofs of the animals that live within.  Each stall has a hay-filled manger mounted along the wall beside a water bucket, and blankets and saddles are flung over the partitions."],"exits":[{"to":251,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":231,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":252,"exit":"go","move":"go room"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Horses"]},
  {"id":251,"x":-380,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Stable","descriptions":["At the end of the stables, the air is redolent with the fragrance of fresh hay and oiled leather, and the ring of iron-shod hooves against the stone floor echoes about the building.  The last stall holds no horses.  Instead, it's used as the office of the stablemaster, Sasha, who works at a low table mounted against the wall."],"exits":[{"to":250,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":252,"x":-370,"y":160,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Tack Room","descriptions":["A lean woman with weathered skin, Hostler Garnett rules over the tack room of the Keep's stables, offering everything from spare bridles to an apple to treat a favored horse.  Her leather palm thimble and awl are always in use as she works to mend an old bridle or replace the padding in a worn saddle, muttering all the while about the carelessness of the riders."],"exits":[{"to":250,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Tack Room","Garnett"]},
  {"id":253,"x":-410,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Great Hall","descriptions":["The great hall is expansive with a soaring ceiling of intersecting beams and rafters.  Three candle-laden iron chandeliers provide illumination, and light reflects softly off the polished inlaid wood floor.  Backed benches are the only furnishings, easily arranged for any ceremony upon the dais at the west end of the hall.","The great hall is expansive with a soaring ceiling of intersecting beams and rafters.  Three large arched windows and three iron chandeliers provide illumination, and light reflects softly off the polished inlaid wood floor.  Backed benches are the only furnishings, easily arranged for any ceremony upon the dais at the west end of the hall."],"exits":[{"to":254,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":234,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":259,"exit":"go","move":"go pantry"},{"to":267,"exit":"go","move":"go dais"}],"aliases":["Manor"]},
  {"id":254,"x":-400,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Hallway","descriptions":["Wide and spacious, the main hallway accommodates guests and those on official business at the manor.  Iron sconces for illumination are interspersed with long benches and an occasional decoration on the wall -- a painting of game and autumn fruit, a battered shield with unusual workmanship, an oval mirror within a mistwood frame."],"exits":[{"to":255,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":253,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":261,"exit":"go","move":"go door"}]},
  {"id":255,"x":-390,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Hallway","descriptions":["Wide and spacious, the main hallway accommodates guests and those on official business at the manor.  Iron sconces for illumination are interspersed with long benches and an occasional decoration on the wall -- a painting of a young woman with fair hair, weapons, and a shelf with decorative jars."],"exits":[{"to":254,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":256,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":262,"exit":"go","move":"go arched door"},{"to":264,"exit":"go","move":"go plain door"}]},
  {"id":256,"x":-400,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Hallway","descriptions":["A bend in the hallway connects the public portion of the manor to the area housing retainers and others in their private apartments.  The plaster between the framed timber walls is a warm ocher color and a thick wool runner covers the floor planks to deaden noise.  Sconces provide additional light along the length of the hall towards the north.  Although simple and sturdy, the decor is pleasing and comfortable, an excellent balance between practical and aesthetic."],"exits":[{"to":257,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":255,"exit":"east","move":"east"}]},
  {"id":257,"x":-400,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Hallway","descriptions":["Several private apartments within the manor are accessible from this hallway, a quiet wing off from the primary public area.  Mostly bare, except for the thick carpet covering the wide planked floor and an occasional wall hanging, the peace is broken only by an infrequent shout from beyond the manor confines or a scurrying domestic maid going about her duties."],"exits":[{"to":258,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":256,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":258,"x":-400,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Hallway","descriptions":["At the end of the hallway is a shuttered casement window.  Beneath it, a clay pot with a cascade of scented geraniums flourishes -- their green leaves and pale pink blossoms a refreshing contrast to the practical design of the house.  Similar doors, individualized by small brass plates, lead to the private apartments of retainers and residents.","At the end of the hallway is a casement window with a shutter to increase or limit the spill of light.  Ochre plaster walls glow from the warm daylight, and a clay pot of scented geraniums flourishes -- their green leaves and pale pink blossoms a refreshing contrast to the practical design of the house.  Similar doors, individualized by small brass plates, lead to the private apartments of retainers and residents."],"exits":[{"to":257,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":259,"x":-410,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Butler's Pantry","descriptions":["Silver and gold serving dishes stand behind iron-barred glass doors in a heavy cabinet along one side of the corridor.  For everyday use, stacks of wooden platters lie beside flatbread trenchers atop a low table conveniently located beside the entrance to the great hall, ready to be snatched up when needed.  A small hearth keeps food warm until it's ready to be served."],"exits":[{"to":253,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":260,"exit":"go","move":"go passage"},{"to":260,"exit":"go","move":"go kitchen"}],"aliases":["Butler's Pantry"]},
  {"id":260,"x":-410,"y":70,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Kitchens","descriptions":["Bread dough rises in covered baskets beside the hearth, out of the way of the servants who bustle from job to job in the kitchens.  Pots of fragrant soup and nut porridge simmer over the fire, a joint of meat turns slowly on its spit as it roasts, and the ingredients for some kind of rice dish lie sprawled across one of the tables.  A stone sink near the doorway is empty now, though buckets of coarse sand and water sit nearby, ready for washing dishes after meals."],"exits":[{"to":234,"exit":"out","move":"out","hidden":true},{"to":259,"exit":"go","move":"go passage"}],"aliases":["Kitchens"]},
  {"id":261,"x":-400,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Steward's Office","descriptions":["Organization of the office bodes well for the future of the manor.  The person in charge of the financial and daily affairs of the manor and keep appears to be meticulous in detail -- a shelf behind his work table contains various lists and accounts.  The room itself is inviting, with clean rugs underfoot, a comfortable settee in front of a mullioned window that looks out over the courtyard, and several chairs for those attending to business with the steward."],"exits":[{"to":254,"exit":"go","move":"go door"}],"aliases":["Steward's Office"]},
  {"id":262,"x":-390,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Armory","descriptions":["Shelves and bins line the walls, broken only by arched mullioned windows, and form rows and columns like soldiers ready for deployment.  Chain, scale, and plate armor in varying sizes are ready and polished for service, and a wide variety of offensive weapons, particularly longswords and halberds, are edged and gleaming.  This armory is ever ready for any unexpected attack upon Rossman's fortress."],"exits":[{"to":255,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":263,"exit":"go","move":"go storeroom"}],"aliases":["Armory"]},
  {"id":263,"x":-390,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Storeroom","descriptions":["Disorder has taken hold in the small storeroom, with no apparent system for organization.  Broken weapons and less than perfect armor are crammed in crates ready to be returned to the forge.  Many items look quite serviceable, but have nevertheless failed to meet the required standards."],"exits":[{"to":262,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":262,"exit":"go","move":"go door"}]},
  {"id":264,"x":-390,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Constable's Office","descriptions":["Simple, no-frills, stark even -- the Constable's main headquarters features a desk, chair and chest.  A single window high above is barred.  Muffled sounds come from below the floor."],"exits":[{"to":255,"exit":"go","move":"go door"}],"aliases":["Constable's Office"]},
  {"id":265,"x":-370,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Sticks and Stones, Slings and Supplies","descriptions":["Staff slings and bows hang on the back wall of the shop, carefully displayed to highlight the work of the craftsman who made them.  From time to time, the sound of a stone thudding against the side of the building marks the prowess of some young guardsman practicing against the targets outside."],"exits":[{"to":235,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Sticks and Stones","Slings and Supplies"]},
  {"id":266,"x":-353,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Cabinet Maker's Workshop","descriptions":["Fragrant wood shavings and sawdust litter the corners of the cabinet maker's shop.  The center of the room is used to display the craftsman's art to the discerning home-owner."],"exits":[{"to":247,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Cabinet Maker's Workshop"]},
  {"id":267,"x":-420,"y":50,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Great Hall Dais","descriptions":["Neither large nor ornate, the dais nevertheless is befitting a ruler.  Two steps above the floor of the Great Hall, it has room for a table for honored guests, but at present only two massive chairs are pushed against the back wall.  Creamy linen drapes curtain the area, hanging from a carved wood header above."],"exits":[{"to":268,"exit":"go","move":"go gallery"},{"to":253,"exit":"go","move":"go hall"}],"aliases":["Dais"]},
  {"id":268,"x":-420,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Manor, Musicians Gallery","descriptions":["Raised and screened from the dais along the northern side of the hall, this small gallery is well equipped for musicians' needs.  The plaster walls are hung with a thick tapestry to keep out chilling drafts.  There are several benches and stands for music, as well as storage cabinets to house spare resin, strings, and cleaning cloths."],"exits":[{"to":267,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["Musicians Gallery"]},
  {"id":269,"x":-270,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Smokehouse","descriptions":["A smoky fire smolders in a brazier at the center of the smokehouse, surrounded by racks of butterflied fish stacked on the ground, and hams and sausages hanging from the rafters.  The dense smoke coils around the meat, scenting and drying it for long storage against lean times."],"exits":[{"to":238,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"aliases":["Smokehouse"]},
  {"id":270,"x":-270,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Weaponsmith's Shop","descriptions":["With a dirt floor and roughly finished wooden walls, not to mention the crudely darned breeches hanging from the edge of the apprentices' sleeping loft above, the shop will never win prizes for its charm.  But Lord Rossman has long been known for his skill as a blacksmith, and he and his journeymen offer a fine selection of halberds and longswords to customers who visit his Keep."],"exits":[{"to":228,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Weaponsmith's Shop"]},
  {"id":271,"x":-300,"y":130,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Dyer's Cottage","descriptions":["Fleeces in all colors of the rainbow hang, lashed to wooden stretcher frames, from the walls of the tiny cottage.  Brilliant arrays of dyed fabrics in carefully folded stacks line the shelves along the walls, ready for customers to collect the work they commissioned."],"exits":[{"to":246,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Dyer's Cottage"]},
  {"id":272,"x":-120,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Gretzyl the Herbalist's Cottage","descriptions":["Herb-filled cheesecloth bags, waxed-covered cheese and spicy string-bound sausages hang from the rafters to dry, filling the cottage with a delicious fragrance.  A wooden potting bench along the back wall holds the implements of the herbalist's profession -- weights and measuring scales, a shallow wooden mortar, some empty earthenware jars and jugs of sweet oil."],"exits":[{"to":187,"exit":"out","move":"out"}],"color":"#FF0000","aliases":["Gretzyl the Herbalist's Cottage","Herbs"]},
  {"id":273,"x":-340,"y":10,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, North Tower","descriptions":["Fresh hay strewn over the rough floor of the tower freshens the air despite the close quarters and lingering scents of oiled metal, leather and sweat.  Weapons hang on the walls and a vellum nailed to a post is marked with names and x's designating officers on watch duty.  Beside the door are a bucket of fresh water and a barrel of apples."],"exits":[{"to":236,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":274,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"}]},
  {"id":274,"x":-340,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, North Tower","descriptions":["The upper room of the north tower opens east and west onto the wooden ramparts.  Its octagonal roof is supported by thick beams from which dangle ropes and hooks to keep extra provisions in the rafters overhead.  Iron-banded chests line the walls as storage for weapons, ammunitions and armor as well as seats for weary guards.  Light pierces through a narrow window which looks out to the northern reaches of Mistwood Forest beyond the nearby fields and the northern section of the town below the motte."],"exits":[{"to":285,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":275,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":273,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"}],"aliases":["North Tower"]},
  {"id":275,"x":-370,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Northwest Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the northern wall of the wooden parapet are interspersed with an occasional hinged shutter that opens for a better view of the territory below.  A slanting tiled roof overhead protects from weather and potential raining projectiles, and a railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side.  A solid wall forms a barrier below the railing, perhaps in response to any stray arrow from the archery field in the bailey below."],"exits":[{"to":276,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":274,"exit":"go","move":"go tower"}]},
  {"id":276,"x":-400,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Northwest Wall Walk","descriptions":["The northwest corner of the allure is wider as the walkway cantilevers out over the wall for a better view of both the lake to the west and the nearby fields and forest to the north.  A bench built into the rampart provides a step up to peer out and a spot to view the intersecting walkways, but the roof of the manor house blocks the southeastern view.  Overhead, a slanted tile roof protects from weather and projectiles, and a railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side."],"exits":[{"to":275,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":277,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":277,"x":-450,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Western Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the western ramparts reveal the expanse of Lake Gwenalion at the bottom of the high cliff that guards the western edge of Rossgallan Keep.  A slanting tiled roof overhead protects from weather, and a railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side.  Looking towards the courtyard is the back of the manor house with a narrow rear yard behind it.  Roofs of storage sheds are visible directly below."],"exits":[{"to":276,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":278,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":278,"x":-450,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Western Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the western ramparts reveal the expanse of Lake Gwenalion at the bottom of the high cliff that guards the western edge of Rossgallan Keep.  From this point to the north, the wall walk runs behind the manor house, enclosing it completely within the high walls.  A slanting tiled roof overhead protects from weather, and a railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side."],"exits":[{"to":277,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":279,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":279,"x":-450,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Western Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the western ramparts reveal the expanse of Lake Gwenalion at the bottom of the high cliff that guards the western edge of Rossgallan Keep.  Although unlikely any attackers could scale the steep cliff from the lake, a ladder leads up to a lookout platform overhead to monitor any unusual activity on the lake.  A railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side, with the back and the thatched-roof of the chapel visible below."],"exits":[{"to":278,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":280,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":284,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"}]},
  {"id":280,"x":-450,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Western Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the western ramparts reveal the expanse of Lake Gwenalion at the bottom of the high cliff that guards the western edge of Rossgallan Keep.  A slanting tiled roof overhead protects from weather, and a railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side.  The familiar odors and sounds from the stable pens below fill the air."],"exits":[{"to":279,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":281,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":281,"x":-450,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Western Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the western ramparts reveal the expanse of Lake Gwenalion at the bottom of the high cliff that guards the western edge of Rossgallan Keep.  The crumbling and jagged cliff rocks are bare but for a rare tree or shrub struggling to grow amongst them.  The slanting tiled roof overhead protects from weather, and the view of the courtyard below reveals the jousting fields, stables, kennels and mews housed in this quadrant of the keep."],"exits":[{"to":280,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":282,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":282,"x":-400,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Southwest Wall Walk","descriptions":["The southwest corner of the allure is wider as the walkway cantilevers out over the wall for a better view of both Lake Gwenalion below to the west and the river mouth to the south.  A bench built into the rampart provides a step up to peer out and a spot to view the intersecting wall walks leading north and east.  Overhead, a slanted tile roof protects from weather and any unlikely projectile.  Beyond a safety railing on the courtyard side is a view of the roofs of the stables and animal pens."],"exits":[{"to":283,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":281,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":283,"x":-370,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Southwest Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the southern wall of the wooden parapet are interspersed with an occasional hinged shutter that opens for a better view of the river mouth below.  A slanting tiled roof overhead protects from weather and raining projectiles, although the southwest section of the keep is additionally guarded by the high cliffs where the Jantspyre flows into the lake.  The railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side, where the familiar sounds and odors of horses mingle."],"exits":[{"to":282,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":296,"exit":"go","move":"go tower"}]},
  {"id":284,"x":-460,"y":90,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Watch Platform","descriptions":["Wind whips across the small platform sheltered by a wooden roof, but the view is spectacular.  To the east and south, beyond Rossman's Landing, the Jantspyre flows to meet Lake Gwenalion, with the Mistwood Forest beyond.  Westward there is a commanding watch of the lake - any suspicious boat activity would be easily tracked from here.  A sturdy railing surrounds the platform, one side whittled with haphazard notches."],"exits":[{"to":279,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"}],"aliases":["Watch Platform"]},
  {"id":285,"x":-310,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Northeast Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the northern wall of the wooden parapet are interspersed with an occasional hinged shutter that opens for a better view of the territory below.  A slanting tiled roof overhead protects from weather and potential raining projectiles, and a railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side.  There is view of the tops of the fruit trees growing to the south over the railing."],"exits":[{"to":286,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":274,"exit":"go","move":"go tower"},{"to":292,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"}]},
  {"id":286,"x":-280,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Northeast Wall Walk","descriptions":["The northeast corner of the allure is wider where the walkway cantilevers out over the wall for a better view of the lands to the north and the town east of the motte.  A bench built into the northeast rampart functions as a step up to peer out over the ramparts and a resting spot with a view down the walkways extending south and west.  Overhead, a slanted tile roof protects from weather and potential raining projectiles, and a railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side."],"exits":[{"to":287,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":285,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":287,"x":-230,"y":30,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Eastern Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the eastern wall of the wooden parapet are interspersed with an occasional hinged shutter that opens for a better view of the town below.  A slanting tiled roof overhead protects from weather and potential raining projectiles, and a railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side.  Visible within the courtyard to the west are the tops of fruit trees and several low, thatch-roofed buildings to the southwest."],"exits":[{"to":288,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":286,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":288,"x":-230,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Eastern Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the eastern wall of the wooden parapet are interspersed with an occasional hinged shutter that opens for a better view of the town below.  A slanting tiled roof overhead protects from weather and any projectiles, and a railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side.  Among the buildings westward within the courtyard is a wooden silo, and the sweet scent of smoke swirls thickly from the smokehouse nearby."],"exits":[{"to":287,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":289,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":289,"x":-230,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Eastern Wall Walk","descriptions":["The keep gate is directly below this section of the allure or wall walk.  Part of the east rampart wall can be opened by a heavy, hinged shutter to allow defenders to attack any invaders below.  Additionally, an iron plate fitted in a hole in the floor may be removed in order to dump noxious materials.  Several well-placed arrow slots, or loops, allow maximum concealed views of any approachers.  The slanted tile roof shelters soldiers from the weather and any projectiles fired in attack."],"exits":[{"to":288,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":290,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":290,"x":-230,"y":120,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Eastern Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the eastern wall of the wooden parapet are interspersed with an occasional hinged shutter that opens for a better view of the town below.  A slanting tiled roof overhead protects from weather and any projectiles, and a railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side.  Within the courtyard to the west are the roofs of several small buildings and shops clustered in the southeast quadrant and up against the eastern wall."],"exits":[{"to":289,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":291,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":291,"x":-230,"y":150,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Eastern Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the eastern wall of the wooden parapet are interspersed with an occasional hinged shutter that opens for a better view of the town below.  A slanting tiled roof overhead protects from weather and any projectiles, and a railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side.  From within the keep, ringing sounds of metal on metal and billows of smoke and flying sparks emanate from a stone building."],"exits":[{"to":290,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":293,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":292,"x":-310,"y":-30,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, North Tower Roof","descriptions":["The gently sloping roof is covered with thin fireproof slates, and the ridge is flattened to hold a huge, shallow tenuated iron basin.  By day the basin is scrubbed, polished and tilted up at an angle to reflect and flash in the sunlight.  By night a massive watch fire burns within it as a beacon, asserting the keep's presence and fortitude.  Smoke and embers at night only add to the ever-present danger of falling off the roof -- those who man the tower roofs must be nimble, alert and diligent."],"exits":[{"to":285,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"}]},
  {"id":293,"x":-280,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Southeast Wall Walk","descriptions":["The southeast corner of the allure is wider as the walkway cantilevers out over the wall for a better view of both the town below to the east and the river to the south.  A bench built into the rampart provides a step up to peer out and a spot to view the intersecting wall walks leading north and west.  Overhead, a slanted roof protects from weather and projectiles.  Beyond a safety railing on the courtyard side is a view of the roofs of small buildings clustered throughout the southeast quadrant."],"exits":[{"to":291,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":294,"exit":"west","move":"west"}]},
  {"id":294,"x":-310,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, Southeast Wall Walk","descriptions":["Arrow loops cut into the southern wall of the wooden parapet are interspersed with an occasional hinged shutter that opens for a better view of the town and river below.  A slanting tiled roof overhead protects from weather and potential raining projectiles, and a railing lends some safety from a misstep along the bailey side.  Smoke, sparks and noise issue from the stone forge below within the courtyard."],"exits":[{"to":293,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":296,"exit":"go","move":"go tower"},{"to":297,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"}]},
  {"id":295,"x":-340,"y":170,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, South Tower","descriptions":["A jumble of crates with straw packing is piled against one wall with a grey-striped cat sleeping curled up in an empty box.  Fine ashes and soot drift through the air from the nearby forge, and a thin coat of grimy dust covers everything, including a keg set upon a makeshift trestle table."],"exits":[{"to":230,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":296,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"}]},
  {"id":296,"x":-340,"y":200,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, South Tower","descriptions":["The upper room of the south tower opens east and west onto the wooden ramparts.  Its octagonal roof is supported by thick beams from which dangle ropes and hooks to keep extra provisions in the rafters overhead.  Iron-banded chests line the walls as storage for weapons, ammunitions and armor as well as seats for weary guards.  Light pierces through a narrow window that looks south towards the juncture of Lake Gwenalion and the Jantspyre River far below."],"exits":[{"to":294,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":283,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":295,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"}],"aliases":["South Tower"]},
  {"id":297,"x":-310,"y":210,"z":0,"title":"Rossgallan Keep, South Tower Roof","descriptions":["The gently sloping roof is covered with thin fireproof slates, and the ridge is flattened to hold a huge, shallow tenuated iron basin.  By day the basin is scrubbed, polished and tilted up at an angle to reflect and flash in the sunlight.  By night a massive watch fire burns within it as a beacon, asserting the keep's presence and fortitude.  Smoke and embers at night only add to the ever-present danger of falling off the roof -- those who man the tower roofs must be nimble, alert and diligent."],"exits":[{"to":294,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ladder"}]},
  {"id":298,"x":-230,"y":210,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Carousel","descriptions":["Thick brick walls give way to a whitewashed plaster foyer.  Little effort was spent on furnishing the building, which contains only a platinum arch guarded by a Dwarven attendant and a small office off to one side."],"exits":[{"to":299,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":185,"exit":"out","move":"out"},{"to":0,"exit":"go","move":"go platinum arch"}],"aliases":["Carousel","Vault"]},
  {"id":299,"x":-230,"y":220,"z":0,"title":"Rossman's Landing, Rundmolen Post Office","descriptions":["Standing in the plain whitewashed room is a low stone counter made from cut stone blocks.  Vast, countless rows of differently sized shelves are behind the counter, and complex Dwarven mechanisms can be heard as they rearrange the package-covered storage.  Clerks shuffle endlessly back and forth between the counters and shelving as they assist patrons with their packaging and mailing needs."],"exits":[{"to":298,"exit":"north","move":"north"}],"color":"#00FF00","aliases":["Post Office","mail"]}
 ],
